TL_AYUDA_RESIDUOS_QUIMICOS;<color=lightblue>Containers with chemical waste must be treated, emptied and cleaned periodically.</color><br><br>
TL_DESECHOS;Machines and waste to be disposed of: {V0190} <br><br>
TL_ASPERSOR;Fire sprinklers to be repaired: {V0191} <br><br>
TL_CALENTADORES_PRESURIZADOR;<b><color=yellow>PRESSURIZER HEATERS</color></b><br><br>Integrity: {V0200}% | Wear: {VW200}% <br><br>
TL_DISPOSICION_FINAL;<b>RADIOACTIVE WASTE</b><br><br>Occupied spent fuel casks: {V0201} <br><br>
TL_AYUDA_NUCLEO;<color=lightblue>Low core integrity may be caused by excessive temperatures and pressures or a lack of wear maintenance. Low core integrity can lead to a loss of coolant, loss of pressurization, release of radiation, and ultimately the destruction of the plant.<br><br>Fuel cells may get stuck inside the core due to thermal expansion.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_BARRAS_DE_CONTROL;<color=lightblue>Low control rod integrity may be caused by long-term exposure to high temperatures inside the core. Low control rod integrity can lead to excessive power levels in the core, possibly leading towards a nuclear accident.<br><br>Damaged rods cannot be repaired by AO: they must be replaced.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_BARRAS_DE_CONTROL_MOTOR;<color=lightblue>The Control Rod Circuit Board may be damaged by excessive power setting. Use a lower wattage setting to prolong the life of the circuit board.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_PRESURIZADOR;<color=lightblue>Low pressurizer integrity may be caused by excessive temperatures and pressures or a lack of wear maintenance. Low integrity can prevent the pressurizer from maintaining pressure on the core and the primary circuit. This may lead to steam buildup and fluctuations in thermal power.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_EVAPORADOR;<color=lightblue>Low Steam Generator integrity may be caused by excessive temperatures and pressures, or a lack of wear maintenance. Low integrity can cause the Steam Generator to explode.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_CONDENSADOR;<color=lightblue>Low Condenser integrity can cause leakages in the secondary circuit, leading to dry circulation pumps and turbine damage.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_TURBINA_GENERADORA;<color=lightblue>Low Turbine integrity is often caused by spinning the turbine with a lack of vacuum in the condenser. Damage will increase as the turbine continues to spin, ultimately leading to turbine failure. Always keep the MSCV closed until the condenser develops a reliable vacuum.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_TURBINA_ELECTRICA;<color=lightblue>Low Turbine Generator integrity is often caused by spinning the turbine with no load, leading to overheating and eventually generator failure. Always ensure that the Generator power is being directed to the transformers or resistor banks.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_GRUPO_ELECTROGENO;<color=lightblue>Low Diesel Generator integrity is often caused by running without electrical load. It can also explode if the fuel pipe remains open while it is running.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_BATERIA_EMERGENCIA;<color=lightblue>Repetitive charging and discharging will reduce the batteries' lifespan.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_RADIACION_AREA;<color=lightblue>Task AO to decontaminate the plant. Wear a hazmat suit before entering a contaminated area, and remain in your suit until the suit and area are decontaminated.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_RADIACION_TRAJE;<color=lightblue>Damaged Hazmat Suits will not provide enough protection from radiation or contamination. Note - AO cannot repair Hazmat suits, they must be replaced.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_TUBERIA;<color=lightblue>Damaged pipes can cause leakages, and may not be able to withstand higher pressures.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_VALVULA;<color=lightblue>A damaged hydraulic valve will be more prone to sticking. This poses a danger to the operation of the plant.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_CABLE;<color=lightblue>Excess electric current can damage the insulation of cables around the plant. This can jeopardize your ability to control the plant, and can possibly expose you to deadly electric shock.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_BIDONES;<color=lightblue>Clean up excess containers to free up storage slots within the plant.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_BOMBA_AGUA;<color=lightblue>Damaged circulation pumps can overheat and get contaminated, jeopardizing the safe operation of the plant. This damage can be costly and disruptive, and can also reduce the overall efficiency of the reactor. Damaged circulation pumps are limited in speed based on their level of damage.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_DESECHOS;<color=lightblue>AO must clean any chemical or fuel waste tanks.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_ASPERSOR;<color=lightblue>If the fire sprinklers are not properly maintained, they may become clogged, damaged, or inoperative, which could lead to a failure of the fire protection system during an emergency.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_CALENTADORES_PRESURIZADOR;<color=lightblue>If the heaters are not properly maintained, they may become damaged or inoperative, which could lead to problems with the regulation of temperature and pressure in the coolant.<br><br>This could result in reduced efficiency and stability of the reactor, and in severe cases, could lead to a loss of coolant and a dangerous power excursion.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_DISPOSICION_FINAL;<color=lightblue>The final disposition of a used radioactive fuel cell refers to the process of safely and securely disposing of the spent fuel that has been removed from a nuclear power plant after it has been used to generate electricity.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_BOMBA_DE_VACIO;<color=lightblue>The Electric Vacuum Pump creates a vacuum inside the condenser by using electricity. It can be damaged if the Retention Tank water level is too low due to insufficient Motive Flow, or too high because SMSI/OMSI are allowing too much water to be retained.</color><br><br>
TL_AYUDA_AIR_EJECTOR;<color=lightblue>The Steam Jet Ejector creates a vacuum inside the condenser using Motive Steam Flow from the Startup Motive Steam Inlet (SMSI) or Operational Motive Steam Inlet (OMSI).</color><br><br>
