O0003;Accomplish
O0004;NEW GOALS
O0005;Press the [O] key to consult your goals
M0;1|Enter the nuclear reactor plant.<br>Access code: {M0O0}@2|Start the internal generator@6|Find the Control Room#0:0:0|false|Admission and recognition
M1;3|Start generating power in the next {M1O3} hours@4|Generate power for {M1O4} hours or more#0:6:0|true|First generation of energy
M2;5|Generate {M2O5}MW of accumulated energy#0:6:0|true|Constant energy
M3;7|Generate {M307}MW of energy for one hour, without interruptions#0:6:0|true|Power peak
M99;99|Complete objectives to earn Prestige Points.#0:0:0|false|Service Compliance 
M100;100|Training#0:0:0|false|Training
E0;Repair damaged power lines
E1;Replace the Control Rods motor controller
E2;Insert the Control Rods at [*]% to stabilize the reactor
E3;Restore the Control Rods motor controller
E4;Turbine offline.<br>Assign a new turbine in the reactor
E5;Start the maintenance protocol
E6;Cooling towers offline (maintenance required)
E7;Reverse the impending meltdown of the reactor core
E8;Insert the Control Rods to 95% or more to stop the fission
E9;Manually open cooling tower circulation valve
E10;Retrieve the stun gun and darts from the received box
E11;Achieve a minimum service compliance of [*]% (@ points)
E12;Achieve a minimum service compliance of [*]% throughout the day (@ points)
E13;Generate power without interruptions for [*] hours (@ points by hour)
E14;Daily Service Summary
E15;Do not use Resistor Banks or Emergency Batteries for [*] hours (@ points by hour)
E16;Do not use AO's help for [*] hours (@ points by hour)
E17;Avoid Emergency Stops throughout the day (@ points)
E18;Generate an energy peak of [%1] MWh from [%2]:00hs to [%3]:00hs (@ points)
E20;Do not use the emergency batteries throughout the day (@ points)
E21;Do not use diesel generators throughout the day (@ points)
E22;Keep circulation pumps below 50% during [*] hours (@ points)
E23;Maintain the integrity of all modules during [*] hours (@ points)
E24;Difference between generated and required energy.
E25;Generate an energy peak of [%1] MWh from [%2]:00hs to [%3]:00hs (@ points)
E100;Internal emergency power generation.
E101;Starts the diesel generator.
E102;Energize the Control Room.
E103;Activates and energizes the reactor control modules.
E104;Adjusts the coolant volume to the operating level.
E105;Adjusts the flow of the coolant inside the core.
E106;Adjusts the flow of the coolant through the condensers.
E107;Adjusts the flow of the coolant to the cooling towers.
E108;Adjusts the volume of coolant inside the Pressurizer to the operating level.
E109;Adjusts the pressure and temperature of the Pressurizer to the operating level.
E110;Insert the control rods completely into the core.
E111;Repair or replace the internal motor that controls the position of the control rods.
E112;Introduce the fuel cell inside the reactor core.
E113;Move a fuel cell from the depot to the reactor core.
E114;Pull the control rods slightly until fission begins inside the core.
E115;Adjusts the reactor operation to stabilize it within the operational range.
E116;Check that the turbines are generating the minimum operating range of energy.
E117;Verify that the plant is connected to the external network and delivering the generated energy.
E118;Disable internal emergency power generation.
E119;Adjusts the volume of coolant inside the Steam Generators to the operating level.
E120;Turn on at least one diesel generator or verify that there are charged emergency batteries.
E121;Activate the coolant charge pump of the condensation circuit.
E122;Activate the circulation pump of the condenser coolant circuit.
E123;Activate the coolant circulation pumps between the condenser and the evaporators.
E124;Open the evaporator drain valve if the temperature is too high or if it is necessary to reduce it more quickly.
E125;Fuel cell removal.
E300;Enter the plant.
E301;Access the Control Room on the first floor.
E302;Use your tablet to turn on AO and explore its capabilities.
E303;Visit the Reactor Core Room to familiarize yourself with its components.
E304;Visit Internal Supply to visit AO's charging pad, storage racks, and power components.
E305;Visit the Secondary Building where the condenser and turbines are installed.
E306;Visit the Diesel Generator building and understand its fuel system.
E700;Maintain power generation without interruption for [*] hours and meet the required service level.
E701;Maintain power generation without interruption until the storm passes and meet the required level of service.
E702;Restart the plant and start generating power for at least an hour.
