IN039;CONTINUE GAME
IN040;If you continue previous progress, you will lose the Prestige Points recovered from your last playthrough. These points are only available when starting a new game. Are you sure you want to continue with a saved game?
AY001;Movements@To walk through the game world, press the [W] [A] [S] [D] keys.<br>If you want to run, hold down the [SHIFT] key.\n\nTo see around, move the mouse in the direction you want.\n\nWhen you run, your vitality decreases.<br>To recover, stop running for a few seconds.<br>If your health is low, you will not be able to recover and your movements will be slow.\n\nTo know your objectives, press the [O] key and access your tablet.@Ayuda01
AY002;On-screen indicators@On the screen you will be able to see all the time your level of health, fatigue and, if you are wearing a protective suit, the protection level of the suit.\n\nHealth decreases if you fall from one considerable height, if you approach fire or explosions, if you are attacked or if you walk in a radioactive area.<br>The level of fatigue increases the longer you are awake, running or wearing a protective suit.\n\nTo regain health and reduce your fatigue, you must sleep.<br>In the control room there is a room for the Reactor Operators.@Ayuda02
AY003;Switches, Keyboards and Knobs@To operate a switch, click with the left mouse button on the switch you want.<br>In the case of keyboards, in addition to pressing the buttons with the left mouse click, you can use the physical keyboard of your PC and enter the numbers [0] to [9].\n\nTo operate a knob, click with the left mouse button on the knob and while holding it, move the pointer left or right to increase or decrease the value.\n\nYou must be less than one step away to interact with the switches, keyboards or knobs.@Ayuda03
AY004;Object manipulation@Left-click on the object you want to collect: fuel cans, batteries, etc.\n\nTo place an object in a container, or to use it, click the left mouse button again over the object container (while holding it).\n\nTo drop an object, click with the right mouse button.\n\nBe careful where you drop the objects, it might be impossible to retrieve them.@Ayuda04
AY005;Operational Assistant (AO)@AO is designed to maintain the plant's equipment and infrastructure, and provide operational assistance in controlling the reactor.<br><br>AO complements and extends your functionality as plant operator. For example, AO can repair the core, fix power cables anywhere in the plant, and decontaminate rooms. However, AO cannot perform certain tasks that only you can do, such as replace Resistor Blocks, control Manual valves and flip Transformer breakers.<br><br>AO's battery will discharge as it performs tasks. It can return here to recharge. However, if AO gets wet, you must carry AO to the charging pad so it can dry off.@Ayuda05
AY007;Emergency Backup Batteries@These Class A lead batteries provide short-term backup power until Diesel Generators can start providing power.<br><br>A full set of batteries is needed to pass an audit.@Ayuda07
AY008;Short circuit@The cables that carry electrical energy and interconnect the plant need constant maintenance and revision.<br>A failure in one section could cut off power to an entire module or the entire plant.<br>Depending on the situation, it could be catastrophic.\n\nTo repair the short circuit, operate the Repair Clamp on the damaged power cord.@Ayuda08
AY009;Repair Clamp@All cables used are modular, that means they have the same size, protective cover, capacity and resistance.\n\nThe Repair Clamp was specifically designed to repair minor faults, cuts or shorts on any length.<br>The clamp has the ability to repair the connectors and weld the protective structure, all at the same time.\n\nTo repair the short circuit, operate the Repair Clamp on the damaged power cord.@Ayuda09
AY010;Diesel Fuel@The Diesel Generators require a steady supply of diesel fuel while running. To fill the generator from the external diesel tank on the roof, turn off the generator and open the blue valve. Close the blue valve before restarting.<br><br>To fill the generator from a red fuel container, pick up a red container [LMB], point the mouse cursor towards the filler neck, and press [LMB].@Ayuda10
AY011;Diesel Generators@The Diesel Generator can keep the reactor modules running for two hours with a full fuel tank.<br>It is very important to refuel before the tank is empty, as if the generator stops, it may take up to five minutes for it to start again.\n\nTo start the diesel generator, press the [Start] button.<br>If it has enough fuel, in a few minutes it will have reached the speed necessary to supply power to the plant.<br>During the start-up process, the generator does not deliver power.<br>The power light will stop flashing when the generator has stabilized.@Ayuda11
AY017;Hazmat Suit@Hazardous Materials (Hazmat) suits allow you to work in radiation-contaminated areas while limiting harmful exposure to ionizing radiation. You can change into and out of hazmat suits near the Control Room and in the Decontamination Room.<br><br>When wearing your suit, the health meter in the top-right of your screen will change to a two-bar meter. The inner bar represents your personal body health. The outer bar represents the Hazmat suit's integrity. Your suit will lose radiation protection as it becomes damaged. Damaged suits cannot be repaired.<br><br>Be aware that you can track radioactive contamination wherever you walk. Once the facility is decontaminated, you must then decontaminate your suit before exiting it.@Ayuda17
AY018;Operational Crane@The operating crane of the reactor core allows emergency maneuvers to be carried out on the control rods.<br>In emergency cases where the internal control motors do not work, the crane can be used to push the control rods into the core.\n\nIt is important that you keep in mind that the control rods are very resistant to high temperatures and radioactivity, but not to shocks or twisting.<br>If you destroy a control rod, it will be more dangerous to operate the reactor.<br>If you destroy too many control rods, the reactor will be unusable.\n\nNEVER OPERATE WHEN THE INTERNAL CONTROL ROD DRIVE MOTORS ARE RUNNING.@Ayuda18
AY019;AO Charger Backup Batteries@These Class A lead batteries can charge AO in case of a power outage.<br><br>You can move charged Class A batteries to this rack to charge AO in an emergency.@Ayuda07
AY_NUCLEO;Reactor Core@The reactor core is composed of a concrete container, inside which are the fuel cells, control rods and a cooling circuit.<br>Fissile nuclear fuel is used, through nuclear reactions, to generate the heat that will be transported through a thermodynamic cycle, to produce the movement of alternators that transform mechanical work into electrical energy.\n\nCritical mass is the minimum amount of material necessary for a nuclear chain reaction to take place.@Ayuda_NUCLEO
AY_BARRASCONTROL;Control Rods@They are used to control the nuclear fission reaction.<br>They must be introduced into the reactor core to absorb neutrons, and thus control, and eventually stop the reactor.<br>Precise adjustment of the control rod position allows stable fission management.\n\nIn an emergency, control rods are the first safety barrier, since inserting them 100% can stop nuclear fission.@Ayuda_BARRASCONTROL
AY_COMBUSTIBLE;Fuel@A fuel cell is made up of fissile elements, which allow controlled chain reactions to be generated within the reactor core.<br>A fuel cell must be handled with extreme care, a task that must be entrusted to the Operating Assistant.<br>A spent fuel cell will contain radioactive waste that must be stored properly.\n\nPrimary Fuel: used for general fission.\nSecondary Fuel: used to reach critical mass.@Ayuda_COMBUSTIBLE
AY_MODERADOR;Moderator@It fulfills the function of slowing down the speed of the neutrons produced by fission, so that they have the opportunity to interact with other fissile atoms and maintain the reaction.<br>As a general rule, the lower the speed of the neutron, the greater the probability of fission with other fuel nuclei.<br>A correct amount of moderator ensures greater stability within the core.@Ayuda_MODERADOR
AY_REFRIGERANTE;Heat Exchanger@The nuclear fuel heats the water in the primary circuit, delivering heat by thermal conduction through the cladding that contains the fuel.<br>The water heated by the nuclear fuel passes to a type of heat exchanger called a steam generator, where the heat from the water in the primary circuit is transferred to the water in the secondary circuit to convert it into steam.\n\nIt is very important to control the volume, temperature and speed of the water within the cooling circuit and the heat exchanger.@Ayuda_REFRIGERANTE
AY_GENERADOR;Generating Turbines | Steam Generator@The steam generator is a heat exchanger that transmits heat from the primary circuit, through which the water that is heated in the reactor circulates, to the secondary circuit, transforming the water into water vapor that later expands in the steam turbines, producing the movement of these that at the same time make the electrical generators rotate, producing the electrical energy.<br>By means of a transformer, the electrical voltage is increased to that of the electrical energy transmission network.<br>After expansion in the turbine, the steam is condensed in the condenser, where it gives up heat to the cooling cold water in the cooling towers.<br>Once condensed, it returns to the nuclear reactor to start the process again.@Ayuda_GENERADOR
AY_TORRES_ENFRIAMIENTO;Cooling Towers@Cooling towers are structures designed to lower the temperature of the water.<br>In normal conditions the towers are not operating, since the internal circuit of the Reactor can exchange heat between the core and the turbines without the need for external cooling, but in an emergency, the water course can be redirected toward the towers for accelerated cooling and emergency cooling of the reactor core.@Ayuda_TORRES_ENFRIAMIENTO
AY_SERVICIOEA;Emergency Systems@The Reactor has the following security systems:\n-Recirculation of water to the Cooling Towers.\n-Opening of internal pressure valves.\n-Core Flood and Containment Room.\n-Automatic fire sprinkler system.@Ayuda_SERVICIOEA
AY_SUMINISTROINTERNO;Internal Supply@The Reactors of the Nucleares company do not have an external electrical supply, therefore, before introducing energy into the external electrical network, it must first supply the internal systems.<br>To achieve this, the reactor consists of Generating Sets, which are machines capable of moving an electric generator through an internal combustion engine.<br><br>Emergency batteries maintain vital plant functions for a few minutes—typically long enough for the diesel generators to start.@Ayuda_SUMINISTROINTERNO
AY_MESA_GESTION;Reactor Management@The management panel allows observing the status of the various reactor modules, and initiating maintenance or repair tasks.<br>It also allows the replacement of damaged machines, cleaning of radioactive waste and updating the skills of the Operational Assistant.@Ayuda_MESA_GESTION
AY_PUNTOS_PRESTIGIO;Prestige Points@Prestige Points <sprite=0> can be exchanged for upgrades, debris cleaning, or repairs.<br><br>To earn prestige points, you must meet the objectives requested from the Operations Center.<br><br>In addition, for each prestige point earned, your experience as an operator will increase, allowing you to level up.<br>The higher the level, the greater the complexity of the objectives, but also the greater gain in prestige points.@Ayuda_PUNTOS_PRESTIGIO
AY_MASA_CRITICA;Critical Mass@The reactor core has reached critical mass and fission has stabilized.<br>From this moment on, the core will begin to consume primary fuel, therefore, the reactivity will begin to decrease.\n\nIt is very important that in the next few minutes you progressively withdraw the Control Rods until you find the balance close to operating temperature.<br>If you do not do it in time, the core will completely lose reactivity and you will have to start over.\n\n!ATTENTION! If you withdraw the Control Rods too quickly you could lose control of the fission.@Ayuda_NUCLEO
AY_REACTIVIDAD_PERDIDA;Lost Reactivity@The Reactor core has lost reactivity and it will no longer be possible to maintain fission.<br>The core will not be able to raise its temperature if you maintain the current circulation parameters.\n\nYou should achieve a complete stop, and cool down the core, before trying the startup protocol again.@Ayuda_NUCLEO
AY_PINZA_REPARADORA;Repairing pliers@The cable repairing pliers are designed to fix cables, either live or de-energized, by clamping onto the cable and repairing it internally without cutting or removing any parts.<br><br>The pliers have a specialized head that can strip away any damaged insulation from the cable and create a clean and conductive connection.<br><br>To repair live electrical cables, the pliers must have <b>active resistors</b> and be <b>open</b> at the moment of contact with the damaged cable.<br>If the pliers are not open or do not have resistors, the <b>danger of electric shock and death is inevitable</b>.@Ayuda_PINZAREPARADORA
AY_SALA_CONTROL;Control Room@From the Control Room you can access all reactor modules, review gauges, overall status, alarms, and protocols.<br>You can also operate the reactor in full.\n\nIn the reactor core room you will find a secondary control area to operate the reactor in an emergency.@Ayuda_SALA_CONTROL
AY_INYECTOR;POTASSIUM IODIDE INJECTOR@If your health is affected by radiation, go to the Control Room or Decontamination Module and place your hand in the Potassium Iodide injector. This dose will counteract any radiation that is reducing your health.<br><br>Be aware that you will start taking damage if there is radioactive contamination on your body.@Ayuda_AY_INYECTOR
AY_ANALIZADOR;AREA ANALYZER@The tablet can scan many components for wear and integrity for a small Prestige Point cost. Maintenance Tasks will automatically be added to the tablet.<br><br>Note the Area Analyzer can only scan certain components within 10 meters. Always maintain a safe distance from hot or electrified components.@AyudaANALIZADOR
AY_FISION_REVERTIDA;REVERSED MELTDOWN@You did it! You saved the plant, environment, and yourself. You could've run or died, but you chose to apply your skills to prevent a nuclear catastrophe. Your quick thinking and decisive actions will be taught to future nuclear engineers walking in your shadow.<br><br>In recognition of your heroism and bravery, you will receive a very large Prestige Point bonus. The plant will now be decontaminated.@AY_FISION_REVERTIDA
AYUDA_CONTROL_VALVULAS_DRENADO_TITULO;DRAIN & VENT VALVES
AYUDA_CONTROL_VALVULAS_DRENADO;DRAIN & VENT VALVES@These valves allow excess water to be drained into special storage tanks outside. They also allow excess steam to be vented to the atmosphere.<br><br>1. Closed = <color=red>red</color>. Partially open = <color=yellow>yellow</color>. Fully open = <color=green>green</color>.<br><br>2. Valves can be operated manually by activating the bypass switch on the side of the valve.<br><br>3. AO can repair any stuck valves.@AYUDA_CONTROL_VALVULAS_DRENADO
AYUDA_CONTROL_VALVULAS_TITULO;MAIN VALVE PANEL
AYUDA_CONTROL_VALVULAS;MAIN VALVE PANEL@These valves control the water or steam flowing in the Primary Circuit, Secondary Circuit, and Cooling Circuit.<br><br>1. Closed = <color=red>red</color>. Partially open = <color=yellow>yellow</color>. Fully open = <color=green>green</color>.<br><br>2. Valves can be operated manually by activating the bypass switch on the side of the valve.<br><br>3. A4/B4/C4 are known as "Main Steam Control Valves".<br><br>4. AO can repair stuck valves.<br><br>5. When installing a new loop, valves must be <color=green>opened</color> to avoid pump damage.<br><br>6. Opening RCV when the core is hot will <color=red>damage</color> the Primary Cooling Storage Tank.@AYUDA_CONTROL_VALVULAS
AYUDA_CONTROL_BLINDAJE_TITULO;CONTAINMENT
AYUDA_CONTROL_BLINDAJE;CONTAINMENT@Ionizing radiation can make you very sick in this game. You can also spread radioactive contamination around the plant.<br><br>This facility was designed with multiple redundant layers of concrete, lead, and steel to prevent ionizing radiation or high-energy neutrons from harming you or the environment.<br><br>A serious radiological accident can occur if the Containment integrity is lost. In this game, the National Atomic Energy Commission (NAEC) is responsible for upholding nuclear safety standards for your protection and the long-term protection of the environment.@AYUDA_CONTROL_BLINDAJE
AYUDA_CONTROL_RESIDUOS_TITULO;SPENT FUEL DISPOSAL
AYUDA_CONTROL_RESIDUOS;SPENT FUEL DISPOSAL@High-level nuclear waste is very toxic to the operator and to the surrounding environment. It must be transported and disposed of in a controlled, responsible manner.<br><br>This plant includes a crane gripper that can safely transport spent fuel cells from the core to its storage cask in the Fuel Depot. The crane can be operated remotely via the tablet's "Operational Tasks" app, minimizing physical risks to the operator.<br><br>Disposed fuel cells can no longer be reused.@AYUDA_CONTROL_RESIDUOS
AYUDA_CONTROL_COMBUSTIBLE_TITULO;FUEL CELLS
AYUDA_CONTROL_COMBUSTIBLE;FUEL CELLS@New fuel cells are stored in the Fuel Depot above the Reactor Core Room. Up to eight new fuel cells can be purchased in the tablet's "Supplies and Spare Parts" app. It is safe to stand next to a new, undamaged fuel cell because it is not yet emitting any high-level radioactive byproducts.<br><br>The NAEC has approved the use of Class B and Class C fuel cells in this reactor. Class C blocks burn stronger but faster than Class B blocks. Researchers are still discovering why Class C fuel cells seem to strengthen each other when installed together.@AYUDA_CONTROL_COMBUSTIBLE
AYUDA_CONTROL_PRESURIZADOR_TITULO;PRESSURIZER
AYUDA_CONTROL_PRESURIZADOR;PRESSURIZER@The pressurizer (PZR) is a key component in a Pressurized Water Reactor plant. The PZR maintains the pressure across the entire primary system to prevent primary coolant water from boiling away.<br><br>This plant has a thermometer to keep pressure levels in the operating range. AO can also maintain the pressure levels if necessary.<br><br>A sudden loss of pressure can cause primary water to rapidly evaporate into steam. Hot fuel cells in the core can melt down if they are no longer cooled. Therefore, the pressurizer must remain online and in good condition when the reactor is operating.@AYUDA_CONTROL_PRESURIZADOR
AYUDA_CONTROL_SUMINISTRO_TITULO;INTERNAL POWER DISTRIBUTION
AYUDA_CONTROL_SUMINISTRO;INTERNAL POWER DISTRIBUTION@The plant's internal electrical system can be powered by one of four sources. The circuit breakers for these sources can be found in the back of the 2nd floor Internal Supply Room.<br><br><b>1. Turbine Generators:</b> By default, the turbine generators will power this plant when the turbine is rotating.<br><br>2. <b>External Power Source:</b> The plant has a secondary, low-voltage connection to the city grid. The city charges a small, daily fee which can be paid or auto-paid in the BANK AND INVOICES tablet app. The city may disable this connection for maintenance or non-payment of power bills.<br><br><b>3. Diesel Generators:</b> The plant has space for up to two diesel generators and up to 10 red fuel canisters, and an additional gravity-fed fuel tank on the roof of the Diesel Generator Building for long-term outages. Never operate the diesel generators with the fuel tank valve open.<br><br><b>4. Emergency Battery Backup:</b> The plant has an emergency battery rack, with space for up to four batteries in case of a short-term power loss.@AYUDA_CONTROL_SUMINISTRO
AYUDA_CONTROL_NUCLEO_TITULO;REACTOR CORE
AYUDA_CONTROL_NUCLEO;REACTOR CORE@The reactor core is where nuclear fission occurs.<br><br>Fuel Cells contain various isotopes of Uranium, including a small percentage of U-235. When a U-235 nucleus absorbs one more neutron, it will fission (split apart), releasing heat and 2-3 more neutrons.<br><br>Control Rods absorb neutrons, slowing down the rate of fission. Control Rods can be withdrawn from the core to increase the rate of fission and heat.<br><br>Water slows down neutrons so that they can be absorbed by a U-235 nucleus, maintaining the chain reaction of nuclear fission. Water also carries away heat to the Steam Generators.@AYUDA_CONTROL_NUCLEO
AYUDA_CONTROL_BDC_TITULO;CONTROL RODS
AYUDA_CONTROL_BDC;CONTROL RODS@Nuclear power plants use Control Rods and Boron to dramatically slow down the rate of nuclear fission. Additionally, Iodine and Xenon will further slow down the reaction.<br><br>In case of an emergency, the control rods can be inserted fully into the reactor core to stop the fission chain reaction.<br><br>Note - Boron, Iodine, and Xenon are available after activating Chemical Module at the start of a new game.@AYUDA_CONTROL_BDC
AYUDA_CONTROL_TURBINAS_TITULO;EXTERNAL ENERGY DISTRIBUTION
AYUDA_CONTROL_TURBINAS;EXTERNAL ENERGY DISTRIBUTION@The goal of this game is to balance the plant's power generation with the city grid's demand.<br><br>Steam spins a turbine which is connected to an electrical generator. The Generator produces Alternating Current electricity which is sent to the Transformers or Resistor Banks. Some of this electricity is used to internally power the plant.<br><br>However, too much of anything can be a bad thing. The city can disconnect the transformers if demand is not met. Overloaded electrical components can burn out, catch fire, or explode. You must carefully manage this energy balance while ensuring that the components remain in good condition.@AYUDA_CONTROL_TURBINAS
AYUDA_CONTROL_REFRIGERANTE_TITULO;COOLANT
AYUDA_CONTROL_REFRIGERANTE;COOLANT@This reactor design uses fresh ocean water in its primary, secondary, and cooling circuits. Water is free, infinitely plentiful around the facility, and filtered for any marine wildlife.<br><br>This plant has two types of pumps:<br><br><b>Freight Pumps</b> allow water to be loaded or unloaded into the Primary, Secondary, and Cooling circuits.<br><br><b>Circulation Pumps</b> are designed to continuously pump water within these circuits.@AYUDA_CONTROL_REFRIGERANTE
AYUDA_CONTROL_EVAPORADOR_TITULO;STEAM GENERATORS
AYUDA_CONTROL_EVAPORADOR;STEAM GENERATORS@The Steam Generator connects the Primary and Secondary systems. It has a cavity filled with secondary water, and a series of tubes filled with very hot, pressurized primary system water.<br><br>During startup, the secondary water boils at 100°C, and its boiling point will further increase as pressure builds. Once at operating pressure and temperature, any decrease in pump speed will cause pressure to increase, and vice versa.<br><br>This plant has three Steam Generators configured in three parallel loops. Each steam generator has pressure vents to release steam pressure and stop condensation when shutting down.@AYUDA_CONTROL_EVAPORADOR
AYUDA_CONTROL_CONDENSADOR_TITULO;Condenser
AYUDA_CONTROL_CONDENSADOR;Condenser@The condenser in a thermal plant allows steam to be reused as liquid water. Once steam condenses into water, it can be reused by the secondary pumps in an infinite Rankine Cycle.<br><br>The interior of the condenser has tubes filled with cold water. This water is chilled by the two natural draft Cooling Towers.<br><br>The condenser's vacuum system makes it much easier for hot steam to condense into water droplets. However, a loss of vacuum can cause condenser water to quickly evaporate into steam. Secondary pumps can run dry if water level falls extremely low.@AYUDA_CONTROL_CONDENSADOR
AYUDA_PLAN_ESCAPE_TITULO;TRAIN ESCAPE
AYUDA_PLAN_ESCAPE;Train Escape@You have survived the meltdown, but the plant and the island were both destroyed.<br><br>You can start a new game with 50% of your Prestige Points, Experience, and Operating Level. If you continue a previous saved game, you will not receive any additional rewards.@AYUDA_CONTROL_NUCLEO
