NV00P;To report bugs, comments, or make suggestions, press the F12 key or email me at "nuclearlastdarkness@gmail.com", or in the Steam Community.<br>All comments are welcome and helpful!
NV00T;Release notes:
NV001;A 0.0.06.122: New FREE game MODE! Now you have the reactor completely at your disposal to do whatever you want.<br>Included in this version are the main objectives to be met in order to earn prestige points that can be redeemed to repair or replace damaged components.
NV002;In addition, great graphical improvements have been added: full day and night cycle, motion effects, depth of field, realistic reflections, outdoor visual effects.<br>And a General Control Console to observe the different areas and control repairs.<br>New fire-fighting system.
NV003;
NV004;
NV005;
T_CONTENEDOR_DELIVERY;CONTAINER
D_CONTENEDOR_DELIVERY;Purchases made are delivered in protective containers.
T_GEN_ENERGIA_GENERADA;ENERGY GENERATED
D_GEN_ENERGIA_GENERADA;Indicates total electrical power generated by all turbines.
T_GEN_TEMP_OPE_ALCANZADA;OPERATING TEMPERATURE REACHED
D_GEN_TEMP_OPE_ALCANZADA;The operating temperature is the lowest level that the turbine needs to start generating power.<br>If the light is flashing, it indicates that the turbine has reached operating temperature and is in stabilization stage.
T_GEN_ESTADO_GENERANDO_LUZ;GENERATING ENERGY 
D_GEN_ESTADO_GENERANDO_LUZ;Indicates that the turbine is stabilized and is generating electrical power.
T_GEN_ENERGIA_GENERADA_NUMERICA;GENERATED ENERGY
D_GEN_ENERGIA_GENERADA_NUMERICA;Indicates the current amount of energy generated by the turbines.
T_GEN_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;INTERNAL TEMPERATURE
D_GEN_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;Indicates the internal temperature of the turbine that will be converted into useful mechanical energy through a thermodynamic expansion transformation.
T_GEN_TEMPERATURA_MINIMA_OPERATIVA;OPERATING TEMPERATURE
D_GEN_TEMPERATURA_MINIMA_OPERATIVA;The operating temperature is the lowest level that the turbine needs to start generating power.
T_GEN_EQ;STABILIZATION LEVEL
D_GEN_EQ;Indicates whether the energy generated by the core is in equilibrium with the thermal energy converted by the turbines.<br>If the indicator shows a deficiency (left), the turbines are converting more energy than the core is producing.<br>If the indicator shows excess (right), the core is generating more power than the turbines can convert.<br>The left green light indicates exchange balance; the right green light indicates thermal balance.
T_GEN_INTEGRIDAD;INTEGRITY
D_GEN_INTEGRIDAD;Indicates the integrity level of the module.<br>Integrity may decline due to excess operation, or wear and tear from normal use.<br>Integrity affects the performance and effectiveness of the module.<br>Too low an integrity is extremely dangerous.
T_GEN_CONECTADO_LUZ;EXTERNAL DISTRIBUTION NETWORK
D_GEN_CONECTADO_LUZ;Indicates if the turbines are connected to the external distribution network.<br>If the turbines are not connected, the energy generated in its entirety will be consumed internally.<br>ATTENTION: Never disconnect the turbines from the external network, except in cases of force majeure where it is necessary to use all of the internally generated energy.
T_GEN_ALTA_PRESION;TURBINE GENERATOR | HIGH PRESSURE
D_GEN_ALTA_PRESION;If the light is on, it indicates that the module has exceeded operating pressure.<br>Too high a level of pressure can cause a reduction in the efficiency of the module, damage to the structure or total destruction.
T_GEN_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;TURBINE GENERATOR | HIGH TEMP
D_GEN_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;If the light is on, it indicates that the module has exceeded operating temperature.<br>Too high a temperature level can cause a reduction in module efficiency, damage to the structure, or total destruction.
T_TecladoNumericoGEN_SET_POT;POWER REGULATOR
D_TecladoNumericoGEN_SET_POT;The keyboard allows you to set the power at which the turbines should operate.<br>To establish the power, indicate the percentage of the maximum capacity.<br>For example, a value of 50% indicates that the turbines will operate at half their maximum capacity.
T_GEN_POS_POTENCIA_ACTUAL;CURRENT POWER
D_GEN_POS_POTENCIA_ACTUAL;Indicates the current power level set and at which the turbines are operating.<br>For example, a value of 50% indicates that the turbines will operate at half their maximum capacity.
T_InterruptorGENERADOR_CONECTAR;CONNECT TURBINES
D_InterruptorGENERADOR_CONECTAR;Indicates whether the turbines should be connected to the external distribution network.<br>If the turbines are not connected, the energy generated in its entirety will be consumed internally.<br>ATTENTION: Never disconnect the turbines from the external network, except in cases of force majeure where it is necessary to use all of the internally generated energy.
T_InterruptorGENERADOR_ENCENDER;SWITCH ON TURBINES
D_InterruptorGENERADOR_ENCENDER;Indicates whether the turbines must be turned on, so that they can begin to convert thermal energy into useful mechanical energy through an expansion thermodynamic transformation.
T_PALANCA;PANEL DISCONNECT
D_PALANCA;Nonessential panels can be powered down when conserving electricity.
T_GEN_SET_POS_POTENCIA;SET POWER
D_GEN_SET_POS_POTENCIA;Press to set the turbine operating percentage entered on the keyboard.
T_GEN_REPARACION_REQUERIDA;TURBINE GENERATOR | MAINTENANCE
D_GEN_REPARACION_REQUERIDA;The active generator turbine needs to be repaired.<br>The integrity is not optimal and the usual maintenance tasks will not be sufficient.
T_0_GEN_POTENCIA_TURBINA_ELECTRICA;TURBINE GENERATOR | POWER
D_0_GEN_POTENCIA_TURBINA_ELECTRICA;Indicates the total power level of the turbine.
T_0_GEN_VELOCIDAD_TURBINA_ELECTRICA;TURBINE GENERATOR | SPEED
D_0_GEN_VELOCIDAD_TURBINA_ELECTRICA;Indicates the rotation speed level of the turbine.
T_GEN_PRESION_TURBINA;TURBINE GENERATOR | PRESSURE
D_GEN_PRESION_TURBINA;Indicates the internal pressure of the generating turbine.
T_GEN_TEMPERATURA_TURBINA;TURBINE GENERATOR | TEMPERATURE
D_GEN_TEMPERATURA_TURBINA;Indicates the internal temperature of the generating turbine.
T_GEN_EXISTE_TURBINA;TURBINE GENERATOR | STATUS
D_GEN_EXISTE_TURBINA;Indicates if the generator turbine is installed and operational.
T_BATERIA;BATTERY
D_BATERIA;Batteries can be stored, supplied with energy or charged in the cabinets of the internal supply area.
D_CABLE;Cables transmit electrical power through the plant.<br><br><b>Danger:</b> if a cable is shorted, do not touch it without first disconnecting the circuit.
T_MonitorSuministroClima;WEATHER MONITOR
D_MonitorSuministroClima;5-Day Weather Forecast. Weather affects energy demand, and may also affect condensation (if enabled in menu options).
T_keyboard;COMMUNICATIONS TERMINAL
D_keyboard;The communications terminal allows saving a report with the status of the plant.<br>In addition, you can load a previously saved report to continue operating the reactor from that point.
T_Terminal;SERVICE SUMMARY
D_Terminal;The service monitor shows the total active connections, the total energy demanded and the energy currently generated by the plant, the percentage of service fulfillment and the statistics with the energy peaks.
T_CajaMonitorFision;STABILIZATION MONITOR
D_CajaMonitorFision;Indicates the internal stabilization factors.<br>NGE: Energy generated by the nucleus.<br>NIS: Emergency core cooling.<br>NIR: Exchange of the core with the coolant.<br>RIS: Emergency Cooling.<br>RIG: Coolant exchange with turbines.<br>GE: Energy generated by the turbines.<br>IMPORTANT: The NGE and GE values must be equal to achieve reactor stability.
T_MarcoDetalleModulos;REACTOR MONITOR
D_MarcoDetalleModulos;Shows the main parameters of each reactor module.
T_SUM_POTENCIA_INTERNA_REQUERIDA_NUMERICA;INTERNAL POWER REQUIRED
D_SUM_POTENCIA_INTERNA_REQUERIDA_NUMERICA;Indicates the total energy required internally by the plant to be able to function in optimal and operational conditions.
T_SUM_POTENCIA_INTERNA_DISPONIBLE_NUMERICA;INTERNAL POWER AVAILABLE
D_SUM_POTENCIA_INTERNA_DISPONIBLE_NUMERICA;It indicates the total internal energy available, both for emergency generation by means of diesel generators or batteries, and for generating turbines.
T_SUM_POTENCIA_EXTERNA_DISPONIBLE_NUMERICA;AVAILABLE EXTERNAL POWER
D_SUM_POTENCIA_EXTERNA_DISPONIBLE_NUMERICA;Indicates the total energy delivered to the external network for distribution.
T_MonitorSuministro;SUPPLY MONITOR
D_MonitorSuministro;This panel summarizes the plant's internal power supply.
T_0_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_INICIANDO;DIESEL GENERATOR 1 STARTUP
D_0_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_INICIANDO;Indicates that <b>Diesel Generator 1</b> is starting up. This process takes a few minutes. Lamp will turn off when the generator is online.
T_1_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_INICIANDO;DIESEL GENERATOR 2 STARTUP
D_1_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_INICIANDO;Indicates that <b>Diesel Generator 2</b> is starting up. This process takes a few minutes. Lamp will turn off when the generator is online.
T_SUM_GENERADORES_POTENCIA_NUMERICO;DIESEL GENERATOR | TOTAL POWER
D_SUM_GENERADORES_POTENCIA_NUMERICO;Power generated by all active diesel generators.
T_ELECTROGENOS_CONSUMO_X_HORA;DIESEL GENERATOR | FUEL CONSUMPTION
D_ELECTROGENOS_CONSUMO_X_HORA;Percent of fuel tank being consumed per hour.
T_0_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_GENERANDO;DIESEL GENERATOR | STATUS
D_0_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_GENERANDO;Indicates that Diesel Generator 1 is on, stabilized, and generating power.
T_1_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_GENERANDO;DIESEL GENERATOR | STATUS
D_1_SUM_ELE_ESTADO_GENERANDO;Indicates that Diesel Generator 2 is on, stabilized, and generating power.
T_SUM_ELE01_GENERANDO_NUMERICO;DIESEL GENERATOR | POWER
D_SUM_ELE01_GENERANDO_NUMERICO;Indicates the total energy currently generated by the diesel generator.
T_1_ELECTROGENO_COMBUSTIBLE;DIESEL GENERATOR 1 | FUEL REMAINING
D_1_ELECTROGENO_COMBUSTIBLE;Indicates the current fuel level of the Diesel Generator 1. The unit will stop when this tank level reaches zero. Operator must manually visit the Diesel Generator Building to refuel the unit.
T_2_ELECTROGENO_COMBUSTIBLE;DIESEL GENERATOR 2 | FUEL REMAINING
D_2_ELECTROGENO_COMBUSTIBLE;Indicates the current fuel level of Diesel Generator 2. The unit will stop when this tank level reaches zero. Operator must manually visit the Diesel Generator Building to refuel the unit.
T_0_SUM_ELE_FUERA_DE_LINEA;DIESEL GENERATOR 1 OFFLINE
D_0_SUM_ELE_FUERA_DE_LINEA;The light on indicates that Diesel Generator 1 is out of service and needs to be repaired.
T_1_SUM_ELE_FUERA_DE_LINEA;DIESEL GENERATOR 2 OFFLINE
D_1_SUM_ELE_FUERA_DE_LINEA;The light on indicates that Diesel Generator 2 is out of service and needs to be repaired.
T_SUM_BAT01_CONSUMO_X_HORA;BATTERY BACKUP | CHARGE/DISCHARGE RATE
D_SUM_BAT01_CONSUMO_X_HORA;Indicates the charge rate or discharge rate of the backup batteries.
T_SUM_BAT01_GENERANDO_NUMERICO;BATTERY BACKUP | LOAD
D_SUM_BAT01_GENERANDO_NUMERICO;Current energy provided by backup batteries.
T_SUM_BAT01_CAPACIDAD_NUMERICO;BATTERY BACKUP | CAPACITY
D_SUM_BAT01_CAPACIDAD_NUMERICO;Total capacity of available backup batteries.
T_SUM_POTENCIA_TOTAL;AVAILABLE BACKUP POWER
D_SUM_POTENCIA_TOTAL;Total power available from diesel generators and backup batteries.
T_SUM_BAT_EMER_CARGA;BACKUP BATTERIES - CHARGE LEVEL
D_SUM_BAT_EMER_CARGA;Indicates the charge level of the emergency batteries.<br>Batteries can be recharged with power from the plant's generating turbines, or replaced manually by the plant operator.
T_SUM_BAT01_ESTADO_CARGANDO;BACKUP BATTERIES - CHARGING
D_SUM_BAT01_ESTADO_CARGANDO;Backup Batteries are recharging from another power source.
T_SUM_BAT01_ESTADO_CONSUMIENDO;BACKUP BATTERIES - DISCHARGING
D_SUM_BAT01_ESTADO_CONSUMIENDO;Backup Batteries are powering the plant. Connect an alternate power source before batteries run out.
D_0_SUM_ELE_DETENER;Remotely stop Diesel Generator 1.<br>If this button is not working, you may need to stop the generator manually.<br><color=red>Warning:</color> To avoid overheating, diesel generators must be switched off if the facility is powered by a different method.
T_0_SUM_ELE_INICIAR;Diesel Generator 1 Startup
D_0_SUM_ELE_INICIAR;Remotely start Diesel Generator 1.<br>If this button is not working, you may need to start the generator manually.<br>Ensure fuel valve is closed prior to startup.
T_1_SUM_ELE_DETENER;Diesel Generator 2 Shutdown
D_1_SUM_ELE_DETENER;Remotely stop Diesel Generator 2.<br>If this button is not working, you may need to stop the generator manually.<br><color=red>Warning:</color> To avoid overheating, diesel generators must be switched off if the facility is powered by a different method.
T_1_SUM_ELE_INICIAR;Diesel Generator 2 Startup
D_1_SUM_ELE_INICIAR;Remotely start Diesel Generator 2.<br>If this button is not working, you may need to start the generator manually.<br>Ensure fuel valve is closed prior to startup.
T_SUM_BAT01_SETMODO;Battery Backup Mode
D_SUM_BAT01_SETMODO;USE: Use backup batteries.<br><br>CHARGE: Charge backup batteries.<br><br>AUTOMATIC: Batteries will be used or charged automatically.
T_NUC_NIVEL_01;LOW OPERATIVE LEVEL
D_NUC_NIVEL_01;Reactor is operating below optimal levels.
T_NUC_NIVEL_02;NORMAL OPERATIVE LEVEL
D_NUC_NIVEL_02;Reactor core is operating at optimal levels.
T_NUC_NIVEL_03;EXCESS OPERATIVE LEVEL
D_NUC_NIVEL_03;Reactor core is operating above optimal levels.
T_NUC_INICIAR;STARTING THE IGNITION PROTOCOL
D_NUC_INICIAR;Pushbutton to start the ignition protocol, if the reactor parameters are correct.<br>If the protocol cannot be started, an alarm will sound and the description of the reason will appear on the system message screen.
T_NUC_DETENER;STOP REACTION
D_NUC_DETENER;This button will initiate the Emergency Stop protocol to stop fission and cool the reactor core.<br><br><color=red>FOR EMERGENCY USE ONLY.</color>
T_NUC_REACTIVIDAD;CORE TEMPERATURE CHANGE
D_NUC_REACTIVIDAD;<color=green>Green</color> indicates a stable temperature.<br><color=yellow>Yellow</color> indicates a controlled gain or loss in temperature.<br><color=red>Red</color> indicates an uncontrolled gain or loss in temperature.
T_NUC_MANTENIMIENTO;MAINTENANCE REQUIRED | CORE
D_NUC_MANTENIMIENTO;Illuminated lamp indicates that reactor maintenance is required.
T_NUC_INTEGRIDAD;INTEGRITY | CORE
D_NUC_INTEGRIDAD;Core integrity can be reduced by normal wear or by exceeding limits.<br>Core integrity loss can lead to a nuclear catastrophe.
T_NUC_TEMP_OPTIMA;OPTIMUM CORE TEMPERATURE
D_NUC_TEMP_OPTIMA;The optimum temperature corresponds to the ideal working temperature of the reactor core.<br>If the core is kept within the operating range, there will be no damage to its integrity, no excess internal pressure, no danger of radioactive release, and fuel consumption will be adequate.
T_NUC_EN_PELIGRO;CORE IN DANGER
D_NUC_EN_PELIGRO;Illuminated lamp indicates that the core is operating beyond safe operating limits.<br>Consult the annunciator panels to identify specific temperature, pressure, integrity, coolant status, and emergency system parameters.
T_NUC_ALCANZO_MASA_CRITICA;CRITICAL MASS REACHED
D_NUC_ALCANZO_MASA_CRITICA;The light on indicates that the reactor core has reached critical mass.<br>Critical mass is the minimum amount of fissile material for a nuclear chain reaction to take place.
T_NUC_REACTIVO;REACTIVE CORE
D_NUC_REACTIVO;The light on indicates that the reactor core is reactive and there is active nuclear fission.<br>Induced nuclear fission is a reaction in which a heavy nucleus, when impacted with neutrons, becomes unstable and decomposes into two nuclei, whose sizes are of the same order of magnitude, with great energy release and the emission of two or three neutrons.
T_NUC_READY;READY FOR STARTUP PROTOCOL
D_NUC_READY;Green light indicates that the reactor is ready for start-up protocol.
T_MonitorNucleo;REACTOR CORE MONITOR
D_MonitorNucleo;The monitor shows the main control parameters of the reactor core, and its current situation.
T_NUC_ALTA_PRESION;HIGH PRESSURE HAZARD
D_NUC_ALTA_PRESION;If the light is on, it indicates that the module has exceeded operating pressure.<br>Too high a level of pressure can cause a reduction in the efficiency of the module, damage to the structure or total destruction.
T_NUC_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;HIGH TEMPERATURE HAZARD
D_NUC_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;If the light is on, it indicates that the module has exceeded operating temperature.<br>Too high a temperature level can cause a reduction in module efficiency, damage to the structure, or total destruction.
T_NUC_VALVULA_SETPOS;CORE VENT POSITION
D_NUC_VALVULA_SETPOS;It allows setting the degree of opening of the internal gas release valve of the reactor core.<br>Opening the valve will reduce internal pressure within the core, however, it may release radioactive steam.<br><br><color=red>FOR EMERGENCY USE ONLY.</color>
T_NUC_VALVULA_POS_ESTABLECIDA;CORE VENT OPENING
D_NUC_VALVULA_POS_ESTABLECIDA;Indicates the degree of opening requested for the core pressure release valve.<br><br><color=red>FOR EMERGENCY USE ONLY.</color>
T_NUC_VALVULA_POS_ACTUAL;CORE VENT OPENING
D_NUC_VALVULA_POS_ACTUAL;Indicates the current openness of the core pressure release valve.<br><br><color=red>FOR EMERGENCY USE ONLY.</color>
T_NUC_VALVULA_ABIERTA;CORE VENT OPEN
D_NUC_VALVULA_ABIERTA;The light turns on to indicate that the core pressure release valve is open.<br>Opening the valve reduces the internal pressure within the core, but at the cost of the release of radioactive gases.<br><br><color=red>FOR EMERGENCY USE ONLY.</color>
T_NUC_TEMP_MAXIMA;MAXIMUM TEMPERATURE OF THE REACTOR CORE
D_NUC_TEMP_MAXIMA;Indicates the maximum temperature at which the reactor core can operate.<br>Beyond that maximum temperature, the accelerated degradation of the integrity of the core begins.<br>IMPORTANT: It is catastrophic to exceed the maximum operating temperature of the reactor core.
T_NUC_TEMP_ACTUAL;REACTOR CORE | INTERNAL TEMPERATURE
D_NUC_TEMP_ACTUAL;Indicates the current temperature of the reactor core.
T_NUC_PRESION_MAXIMA;MAXIMUM REACTOR CORE PRESSURE
D_NUC_PRESION_MAXIMA;Indicates the maximum pressure that the reactor core can withstand.<br>Once this maximum pressure is exceeded, accelerated degradation of the integrity of the core begins.<br>IMPORTANT: Exceeding the maximum operating pressure of the reactor core is catastrophic.
T_NUC_TEMPERATURA;REACTOR CORE | INTERNAL TEMPERATURE
D_NUC_TEMPERATURA;Indicates the current temperature of the reactor core.
T_NUC_PRESION;REACTOR CORE | PRESSURE
D_NUC_PRESION;Indicates the current pressure of the reactor core.
T_PantallaAcciones;STATUS TERMINAL
D_PantallaAcciones;The status terminals show on a screen the response of the pushbuttons or switches operated by the plant operator.
T_MonitorControl;CONTROL ROD MONITOR
D_MonitorControl;The monitor shows the main parameters and the current status of the reactor core control rods.
T_BDC_POS_ACTUAL;CONTROL ROD | HEIGHT
D_BDC_POS_ACTUAL;Indicates the average current height of all installed control rods.<br><br>100% indicates that rods are fully inserted down into the core.<br>0% indicates that rods are fully raised above the core.
T_BDC_INICIAR_AJUSTE;ACTIVATE THE MOVEMENT OF THE CONTROL RODS
D_BDC_INICIAR_AJUSTE;The pushbutton activates the internal motors of the Reactor Core to adjust the Control Rods to the position indicated by the keyboard.
T_PL_BarrasDeControl;CONTROL ROD | INTEGRITY
D_PL_BarrasDeControl;The Reactor Core Control Rod integrity panel displays the integrity status of each control rod.<br>If the light is green, the rod is active and working.<br>If the light is red, the rod has lost its integrity, has been seriously damaged and is not active, or has been destroyed.
T_BDC_VELOCIDAD_DISMINUIDA_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;CONTROL RODS ADJUSTMENT MOTOR AFFECTED
D_BDC_VELOCIDAD_DISMINUIDA_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;The light on indicates that the high temperatures of the Reactor Core have compromised the internal motors that facilitate the adjustment of the rods, or have deformed the rods themselves and therefore the adjustment movements will be much slower than normal.<br>They could even be completely blocked.
T_BDC_TEMPERATURA;CONTROL ROD | TEMPERATURE
D_BDC_TEMPERATURA;Indicates the average temperature of the Control Rods. Excessive core temperatures will damage the rods over time. Rods can be cooled by lowering core temperature or by using boron to control the nuclear reaction.
T_BDC_ABSORCION;CONTROL ROD | ABSORPTION CAPACITY
D_BDC_ABSORCION;Indicates control rods' average ability to absorb neutrons inside the core. Rods may be unable to properly control fission due to damage or misplacement in the core.
T_BDC_INTEGRIDAD;INTEGRITY
D_BDC_INTEGRIDAD;Integrity may decline due to excess operation or due to normal wear and tear. Integrity affects the performance and effectiveness of the module. Components will be destroyed when Integrity reaches 0%.
T_BDC_ESTADOOPERACION_INMOVIL;INTERNAL MOTOR ADJUSTMENT | STATIONARY
D_BDC_ESTADOOPERACION_INMOVIL;The light on indicates that the internal adjustment motor of the Reactor Core Control Rods is not performing any adjustment movement.
T_BDC_ESTADO_MOTORINTERNO;INTERNAL MOTOR ADJUSTMENT | STATE
D_BDC_ESTADO_MOTORINTERNO;The green light indicates that the internal motor for adjusting the Reactor Core Control Rods is operational.<br>Instead, a red light indicates that the motor is out of service and is not operational.
T_BDC_ESTADOOPERACION_AJUSTANDO;INTERNAL MOTOR ADJUSTMENT | ACTIVITY
D_BDC_ESTADOOPERACION_AJUSTANDO;The light on indicates that the internal adjustment motor of the Reactor Core Control Rods is performing adjustment movements.
T_MonitorCumplimiento;SERVICE COMPLIANCE MONITOR
D_MonitorCumplimiento;Delivered electricity compared to city grid demand, by hour.
T_NUC_PLATAFORMA_ALTERNAR;CORE MAINTENANCE PLATFORM
D_NUC_PLATAFORMA_ALTERNAR;The push button allows the platform to be raised or lowered, allowing access to the reactor core when it is outside the shield for maintenance tasks.
T_NUC_PLATAFORMA_ACTIVA;CORE ACCESS PLATFORM | STATUS
D_NUC_PLATAFORMA_ACTIVA;The light indicates if the access platform to the Reactor Core is active and can be raised or lowered.
T_CONTENEDOR_TRAJE;HAZMAT SUIT CONTAINER
D_CONTENEDOR_TRAJE;The container stores one hazmat (hazardous materials) suit.<br>IMPORTANT: If the suit is damaged, it will not be safe to use as it will not be able to protect the operator from surrounding radiation.
T_REMPLAZO_MOTOR_BDC;CONTROLLER | CONTROL ROD MOTOR
D_REMPLAZO_MOTOR_BDC;Replacement of the motor controller board for the reactor core control rods.<br>IMPORTANT: To replace the controller board, the reactor must be idle, and the core not energized.
T_SENSOR_RADIOACTIVIDAD;RADIOACTIVITY SENSOR
D_SENSOR_RADIOACTIVIDAD;This alarm will activate when radioactive contamination is detected anywhere in the plant.
T_LUZ_ALARMA;ALARM LIGHT
D_LUZ_ALARMA;Active alarm indicator.
T_LUZ_BC_ENCENDIDA;PUMP | OPERATING
D_LUZ_BC_ENCENDIDA;The light on indicates that the pump is working.
T_LUZ_BC_ENSECO;PUMP | DRY
D_LUZ_BC_ENSECO;The light on indicates that the pump is working, but there is no fluid inside it and therefore it is running dry, which will significantly reduce its useful life.
T_LUZ_BC_SOBRECARGA;PUMP | OVERLOAD
D_LUZ_BC_SOBRECARGA;The light on indicates that the pump is operating with overload, which means that it cannot propel the fluid, because the outlet tubes are full, which will significantly reduce its useful life.
T_LUZ_BC_ENERGIA;PUMP | POWERED ON
D_LUZ_BC_ENERGIA;The light on indicates that the pump is connected to the electrical network, and that there is sufficient voltage in the network to work.
T_LUZ_BC_ALCANZOVELOCIDAD;PUMP | SPEED TARGET ACHIEVED
D_LUZ_BC_ALCANZOVELOCIDAD;Light on indicates that the pump has reached the ordered speed.
T_LUZ_BC_MANTENIMIENTO;MAINTENANCE REQUIRED | PUMP
D_LUZ_BC_MANTENIMIENTO;The light on indicates that the pump requires maintenance and the capacity of the pump is degraded.
T_LUZ_BC_ENCENDIENDO;PUMP | STARTUP
D_LUZ_BC_ENCENDIENDO;The light stays on during the pump start-up process.<br>During this process, the pump will require adequate oil pressure.
T_LUZ_BC_CONTAMINADO;PUMP | OIL CONTAMINATED
D_LUZ_BC_CONTAMINADO;The light on indicates that the oil tank has been contaminated.<br>DANGER.<br>STARTING THE PUMP MAY CAUSE SEVERE INJURY OR EXPLOSION.
T_BC_INTEGRIDAD;PUMP | INTEGRITY
D_BC_INTEGRIDAD;Indicates the integrity level of the pump.<br>Integrity may decline due to excess operation or low oil pressure.<br>Integrity affects the performance and effectiveness of the pump.<br>Too low integrity is extremely dangerous.
T_BC_PRESION_ACEITE;PUMP | OIL PRESSURE
D_BC_PRESION_ACEITE;Indicates the oil pressure of the pump.<br>During the starting of the pump, if the oil pressure is too low, the pump could suffer from premature wear.
T_BIDON_COMBUSTIBLE;DIESEL FUEL CONTAINER
D_BIDON_COMBUSTIBLE;Fuel can for powering machines and generators.
T_BIDON_ACEITE;MINERAL OIL CONTAINER
D_BIDON_ACEITE;Oil can for lubricating pumps and motors.
T_BOCA_DE_CARGA_COMBUSTIBLE;DIESEL CAN FILLER NECK
D_BOCA_DE_CARGA_COMBUSTIBLE;When holding a <color=red>red</color> diesel can, left-click and hold here to fill this tank. You'll need 3 diesel cans to fill the tank completely.<br><br>The tank will turn from red to white when empty. To clean up empty cans, open your tablet [T key] and click "ORDER PARTS & SUPPLIES" > "DIESEL FUEL" > "CLEAN UP".
T_BOCA_DE_CARGA_ACEITE;MINERAL OIL FILLER NECK
D_BOCA_DE_CARGA_ACEITE;Select an oil can from your inventory [I key] and right click here.
T_PINZA_REPARADORA;REPAIR TOOL
D_PINZA_REPARADORA;The repair tool can be used to repair cables that have been damaged by overvoltage or short circuit.<br>To repair a cable, place the clamp on the damaged area.<br>DANGER: Do not use the clamp on cables with electrical voltage or a short circuit without first cutting off the supply.
T_CAJA_INTERRUPTORES_PUERTA;DOOR SWITCH BOX
D_CAJA_INTERRUPTORES_PUERTA;The box holds the door operation switches.
T_InterruptorControlApertura;AUTOMATIC DOOR OPENING
D_InterruptorControlApertura;In Automatic Opening mode, the door will open when you are nearby. This increases internal power consumption.<br><br>In Manual Opening mode, you must press the door button if you want to open the door.
T_InterruptorControlCierre;AUTOMATIC DOOR CLOSING
D_InterruptorControlCierre;In Automatic Closing mode, the door will close when you are no longer nearby. This increases internal power consumption.<br><br>In Manual Closing mode, you must press the door button if you want to close the door.
T_CAJA_INTERRUPTORES_LUCES;LIGHT SWITCH BOX
D_CAJA_INTERRUPTORES_LUCES;The box houses the operation switches for the sector lights.
T_InterruptorCL;LIGHT SWITCH
D_InterruptorCL;Allows you to manually turn on or off all the lights in the sector.
T_InterruptorCLA;AUTOMATIC SWITCH
D_InterruptorCLA;Allows you to set the automatic operation of the sector lights.<br>The lights will come on when motion is detected, and will turn off when leaving the sector.<br>IMPORTANT: Automatic operation increases internal power consumption.
T_SU_RackBaterias_Emergencia01;EMERGENCY BATTERIES
D_SU_RackBaterias_Emergencia01;The emergency battery rack allows critical plant areas to be kept in operation for a short period of time.<br>IMPORTANT: Do not remove the modules from this rack.
T_SU_RackBaterias_Respaldo01;BATTERY CONTAINER
D_SU_RackBaterias_Respaldo01;The battery container allows you to store loaded or unloaded modules, to be used in any rack.<br>It is recommended to keep the modules always charged to be able to use in an emergency.<br>IMPORTANT: The containers have no connection to the plant.<br>To charge a battery, use the emergency rack.
T_SU_RackBaterias_Respaldo04;BATTERY CONTAINER
D_SU_RackBaterias_Respaldo04;The battery container allows you to store loaded or unloaded modules, to be used in any rack.<br>It is recommended to keep the modules always charged to be able to use in an emergency.<br>IMPORTANT: The containers have no connection to the plant.<br>To charge a battery, use the emergency rack.
T_SU_RackBaterias_AO;OPERATING ASSISTANT EMERGENCY BATTERIES
D_SU_RackBaterias_AO;The emergency battery rack allows AO to charge when there is no other power supply.<br>The rack is exclusive to AO's charging pad, therefore it does not supply power to the plant.
T_MonitorAcciones;AO'S TASK LOG
D_MonitorAcciones;Record of the actions carried out by AO.
T_LuzCaja_ELECTROGENO_01_ESTADO;OPERATING STATUS
D_LuzCaja_ELECTROGENO_01_ESTADO;The light on indicates that the diesel generator is active, stabilized, and generating power.
T_PulsadorBoton_ASIGNAR_REF_A;PRIMARY COOLANT PUMP SELECTOR
D_PulsadorBoton_ASIGNAR_REF_A;Allows you to set how the primary coolant pump is active.<br>In order to make a change, the coolant pump must be idle.
T_PulsadorBoton_ASIGNAR_REF_B;SECONDARY COOLANT PUMP SELECTOR
D_PulsadorBoton_ASIGNAR_REF_B;Allows you to set how the secondary coolant pump is active.<br>In order to make a change, the coolant pump must be idle.
T_REF_ASIGNADO_A;COOLANT | MAIN PUMP
D_REF_ASIGNADO_A;The light on indicates that the main circulation pump of the reactor core cooling circuit is active.
T_REF_ASIGNADO_B;SECONDARY COOLANT PUMP
D_REF_ASIGNADO_B;The light on indicates that the secondary circulation pump of the reactor core cooling circuit is active.
T_REF_VOLUMEN_DISPONIBLE_FA;VOLUME PRIMARY COOLANT
D_REF_VOLUMEN_DISPONIBLE_FA;Primary coolant volume indicator inside the cooling circuit.
T_REF_VOLUMEN_DISPONIBLE_FB;VOLUME SECONDARY COOLANT
D_REF_VOLUMEN_DISPONIBLE_FB;Secondary coolant volume indicator inside the cooling circuit.
T_GEN_INTEGRIDAD_A;INTEGRITY OF THE MAIN TURBINE
D_GEN_INTEGRIDAD_A;Main turbine integrity level indicator.
T_GEN_INTEGRIDAD_B;SECONDARY TURBINE INTEGRITY
D_GEN_INTEGRIDAD_B;Secondary turbine integrity level indicator.
T_GEN_ASIGNADO_A;MAIN TURBINE
D_GEN_ASIGNADO_A;The light on indicates that the primary generator turbine is active.
T_GEN_ASIGNADO_B;SECONDARY TURBINE
D_GEN_ASIGNADO_B;The light on indicates that the secondary generator turbine is active.
T_GEN_ASIGNADO_A_MANT;MAIN TURBINE | IN MAINTENANCE
D_GEN_ASIGNADO_A_MANT;The light on indicates that the main generator turbine is undergoing maintenance.
T_GEN_ASIGNADO_B_MANT;SECONDARY TURBINE | IN MAINTENANCE
D_GEN_ASIGNADO_B_MANT;The light on indicates that the secondary generator turbine is undergoing maintenance.
T_REF_ASIGNAR_GEN_A;PRIMARY COOLING PUMP SELECTOR
D_REF_ASIGNAR_GEN_A;Allows you to set the primary cooling pump as active.<br>In order to make a change, the cooling pump must be idle.
T_REF_ASIGNAR_GEN_B;SECONDARY COOLING PUMP SELECTOR
D_REF_ASIGNAR_GEN_B;Allows you to set the secondary cooling pump as active.<br>In order to make a change, the cooling pump must be idle.
T_SEL_REACTOR_MODO;Operating mode
D_SEL_REACTOR_MODO;Allows you to set the reactor's working mode.<br><br>MAXIMUM - Allows operation beyond normal limits.<br>NOMINAL - Default mode. Choose for startup.<br>SHUTDOWN - Allows pistons to be raised.
T_SAI_REF_BOMBA;FIRE FIGHTING SYSTEM | ACTIVITY
D_SAI_REF_BOMBA;The light on indicates that the water charging pump is active.
T_SAI_REF_ZONA;FIRE FIGHTING SYSTEM | DETECTION
D_SAI_REF_ZONA;The light on indicates that a fire is detected and the system is operational.
T_SAI_REF_BOMBA_NIVEL;FIRE FIGHTING SYSTEM | WATER RESERVE
D_SAI_REF_BOMBA_NIVEL;Water reserve level indicator.
T_SAI_GEN_BOMBA;FIRE FIGHTING SYSTEM | ACTIVITY
D_SAI_GEN_BOMBA;The light on indicates that the water charging pump is active.
T_SAI_GEN_ZONA;FIRE FIGHTING SYSTEM | DETECTION
D_SAI_GEN_ZONA;The light on indicates that a fire is detected and the system is operational.
T_SAI_GEN_BOMBA_NIVEL;FIRE FIGHTING SYSTEM | WATER RESERVE
D_SAI_GEN_BOMBA_NIVEL;Water reserve level indicator.
T_SEA_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | INTERNAL TEMPERATURE
D_SEA_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;Indicator of the internal temperature of the Cooling Towers of the Reactor Core.
T_SEA_ESTADO_INICIADO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | STATUS INDICATOR
D_SEA_ESTADO_INICIADO;The light on indicates that the emergency systems are working.
T_SEA_ENFRIANDO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | COOLING INDICATOR
D_SEA_ENFRIANDO;The light on indicates that the Cooling Towers are reducing the temperature of the Reactor Core Coolant.
T_SEA_VELOCIDAD_ALCANZADA;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | VALVE OPENING REACHED
D_SEA_VELOCIDAD_ALCANZADA;The light on indicates that the valves have reached the target opening.
T_SEA_INTEGRIDAD;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | INTEGRITY
D_SEA_INTEGRIDAD;The meter indicates the degree of integrity of the emergency systems.
T_SEA_VELOCIDAD_CIRCULACION;COOLING VALVE OPENING
D_SEA_VELOCIDAD_CIRCULACION;The regulator sets the opening of the circulation valves on the cooling pumps that divert flow to the cooling towers.<br>The larger the opening, the higher the flow rate and therefore the greater the reduction in temperature of the reactor core coolant.

T_SEA_VELOCIDAD_ACTUAL;COOLING TOWERS | CIRCULATION SPEED
D_SEA_VELOCIDAD_ACTUAL;Indicator with the current speed of circulation of the coolant towards the cooling towers.
T_InterruptorSEA_INICIAR;COOLING THE COOLANT
D_InterruptorSEA_INICIAR;The switch allows starting or stopping the opening or closing of the valves that divert the Coolant from the Reactor Core to the Cooling Towers.
T_InterruptorSEA_INICIAR_SN;COOLING THE COOLANT
D_InterruptorSEA_INICIAR_SN;The switch allows starting or stopping the opening or closing of the valves that divert the Coolant from the Reactor Core to the Cooling Towers.
T_SEA_TEMP_AGUA_NUCLEO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | REACTOR CORE FLOOD
D_SEA_TEMP_AGUA_NUCLEO;Indicator of the temperature of the water used to flood and cool the Reactor Core.
T_SEA_NIVEL_AGUA_NUCLEO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | REACTOR CORE FLOOD
D_SEA_NIVEL_AGUA_NUCLEO;Reactor Core flood level indicator.
T_SEA_INUNDAR_NUCLEO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | REACTOR CORE FLOOD
D_SEA_INUNDAR_NUCLEO;Initiates the emergency flooding of the Reactor Core.
T_SEA_PURGAR_INUNDAR_NUCLEO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | REACTOR CORE FLOOD
D_SEA_PURGAR_INUNDAR_NUCLEO;Starts purging of the water used to flood the Reactor Core.
T_SEA_LUZ_INUNDANDO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | REACTOR CORE FLOOD
D_SEA_LUZ_INUNDANDO;The light on indicates that the Reactor Core is being flooded.
T_SEA_LUZ_PURGANDO;EMERGENCY SYSTEM | REACTOR CORE FLOOD
D_SEA_LUZ_PURGANDO;The light on indicates that the water used to flood the Reactor Core is being purged.
T_MonitorEnergiaGeneradaAcumulada;GENERATED ENERGY MONITOR
D_MonitorEnergiaGeneradaAcumulada;Generated power (<color=blue>blue</color>) versus City Demand (<color=green>green</color>).
T_COM_DESECHAR;FUEL | DISCARD
D_COM_DESECHAR;Remove the spent fuel waste from the reactor core.<br><br>Once removed from the core, it must be transported to a final disposal capsule.
T_COM_CARGAR;FUEL | LOAD
D_COM_CARGAR;Insert the fuel into the reactor core.<br>Note that once the fuel has been inserted, the process of nuclear fission will begin.<br>It is critical to exercise caution and maintain close monitoring of the process to prevent any potential accidents or unforeseen consequences.
T_COM_ESTADO_CARGA_CARGADO;FUEL | LOADED
D_COM_ESTADO_CARGA_CARGADO;The light indicates that there is a fuel cell inside the Reactor Core.
T_COM_ESTADO_CARGA_DESCARGADO;FUEL | EMPTY
D_COM_ESTADO_CARGA_DESCARGADO;The light indicates that there is no fuel cell inside the Reactor Core.
T_COM_ESTADO_ZONA_CARGA;FUEL | IN CARGO AREA
D_COM_ESTADO_ZONA_CARGA;The light indicates that there is a fuel cell located in the Reactor Core charging area.
T_COM_ESTADO_DESECHADO_HABILITADO;FUEL | DISPOSAL ENABLED
D_COM_ESTADO_DESECHADO_HABILITADO;The light indicates that a fuel cell is available for disposal.
T_COM_PRINCIPAL_CANTIDAD;FUEL | QUANTITY AVAILABLE
D_COM_PRINCIPAL_CANTIDAD;Indicates the number of fissile fuel units available within the Reactor Core.
T_COM_CALOR_GENERADO;FUEL | ENERGY FACTOR
D_COM_CALOR_GENERADO;Indicates the energy factor generated in each analysis cycle.
T_COM_TEMPERATURA;FUEL | TEMPERATURE
D_COM_TEMPERATURA;Indicates the temperature of the fuel cell inside the Reactor Core.
T_COM_INTEGRIDAD;FUEL | INTEGRITY
D_COM_INTEGRIDAD;The integrity of the fuel cell can be degraded by wear or by exceeding operating parameters.<br>In either case, too low an integrity can allow the release of radioactive material.
T_COM_PRINCIPAL_CONSUMIENDO;FUEL | CONSUMING
D_COM_PRINCIPAL_CONSUMIENDO;The light on indicates that the fuel is being consumed within the Reactor Core.
T_MonitorEnergiaGenerada;AVERAGE GENERATED ENERGY MONITOR
D_MonitorEnergiaGenerada;The average generated energy monitor shows a graph with the average energy generated by the Turbines in each hour (blue bar) and the average energy delivered to the external distribution network (green mark).

T_PRE_VOLUMEN;PRESSURIZER LEVEL
D_PRE_VOLUMEN;Indicates the level of coolant inside the Pressurizer of the main cooling circuit of the reactor core.
T_PRE_PRESION;PRESSURIZER (PZR) PRESSURE
D_PRE_PRESION;Inside the Pressurizer, a small amount of water is boiled until it reaches operational pressure levels.<br>The pressure inside the PZR is then distributed across the entire primary circuit.<br><br>This pressure ensures that water will not boil inside the primary circuit. Any trapped pockets of steam can cause fluctuations in temperature, power levels, and Iodine/Xenon.
T_PRE_TEMPERATURA;PRESSURIZER TEMPERATURE
D_PRE_TEMPERATURA;Indicates the temperature inside the Pressurizer of the primary cooling circuit of the reactor core.
T_PRE_POWER;PRESSURIZER | HEATERS
D_PRE_POWER;Indicates the power of the Pressurizer heaters.
T_PRE_RT_PRESION;RELIEF TANK | PRESSURE
D_PRE_RT_PRESION;Indicates the pressure inside the relief tank.
T_NUC_METRICAS_FLUJO_ENTRADA_REF;INLET COOLANT FLOW - LITERS PER MINUTE
D_NUC_METRICAS_FLUJO_ENTRADA_REF;Indicates the flow rate of the coolant <b>ENTERING</b> the reactor core vessel.
T_NUC_METRICAS_FLUJO_SALIDA_REF;OUTLET COOLANT FLOW - LITERS PER MINUTE
D_NUC_METRICAS_FLUJO_SALIDA_REF;Indicates the flow rate of the coolant <b>LEAVING</b> the reactor core vessel.
T_BLI_RADIACION_CONTENIDA_NUMERICA;CONTAINED RADIATION
D_BLI_RADIACION_CONTENIDA_NUMERICA;Radiation index contained within the containment structure of the Reactor Core.
T_BLI_RADIACION_CONTENIDA;CONTAINMENT SHIELD | RADIATION
D_BLI_RADIACION_CONTENIDA;Radiation detected outside the reactor core vessel.
T_BLI_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;CONTAINMENT SHIELD | TEMPERATURE
D_BLI_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;Average temperature of the reactor core vessel.
T_BLI_INTEGRIDAD;CONTAINMENT SHIELD | INTEGRITY
D_BLI_INTEGRIDAD;A radiological accident may occur if containment shield integrity is lost. 

T_BLI_RADIACION_CONTENIDA_LUZ;CONTAINED RADIATION
D_BLI_RADIACION_CONTENIDA_LUZ;The light on indicates that radiation has been detected within the containment shield of the Reactor Core. If the level rises beyond the containment capacity, or if the integrity of the shield is not sufficient, a radioactive leak could begin. IMPORTANT: Wear a radiation protective suit when entering the Reactor Core room.
T_BLI_LIBERANDO_RADIACION_LUZ;RADIATION RELEASED
D_BLI_LIBERANDO_RADIACION_LUZ;The lit light indicates that radiation has been detected beyond the containment shield of the Reactor Core. A radioactive leak outside the shield is a high-level emergency. IMPORTANT: Use a protective anti-radiation suit in the vicinity of the Reactor Core and pay attention to the radioactivity sensors in each sector of the plant.

T_GraficoBarrasRadioactividad;CONTAINMENT SHIELD | MILLISIEVERT PER HOUR
D_GraficoBarrasRadioactividad;This graph shows hourly radioactivity levels outside the containment shield.
T_MonitorTiempoGenerando;COMPLIANCE HOURS MONITOR
D_MonitorTiempoGenerando;Number of minutes per hour where compliance was met.<br><br>Compliance must be met for at least 54 minutes to receive Prestige Points for that hour.
T_REF_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;COOLANT SYSTEM | TEMPERATURE
D_REF_TEMPERATURA_INTERNA;Indicator with the internal temperature of the Reactor Core Coolant system.
T_REF_TEMPERATURA_SALIDA;COOLANT SYSTEM | TEMPERATURE
D_REF_TEMPERATURA_SALIDA;Indicator with cooled temperature.
T_REF_FACTOR_ENFRIAMIENTO;COOLANT SYSTEM | COOLING FACTOR
D_REF_FACTOR_ENFRIAMIENTO;Indicator with the conversion factor or capacity of the Reactor Core Coolant system.<br>The factor will be altered by the volume and circulation speed.
T_REF_INTEGRIDAD;COOLANT SYSTEM | INTEGRITY
D_REF_INTEGRIDAD;The integrity of the Reactor Core Coolant system may decrease due to use above the safe operating parameters.<br>In any case, excessive pressure or low integrity can cause loss of coolant.
T_REF_VELOCIDAD_SETPOS;COOLANT SYSTEM | SET CIRCULATION SPEED
D_REF_VELOCIDAD_SETPOS;The regulator sets the speed at which the coolant must circulate within the cooling circuit of the Reactor Core.
T_REF_VELOCIDAD_SETPOS_NUMERICA;PRIMARY PUMP | ORDERED SPEED
D_REF_VELOCIDAD_SETPOS_NUMERICA;Indicates the <b>ORDERED</b> speed of the primary circulation pump.
T_REF_VELOCIDAD_ACTUAL;PRIMARY PUMP | CURRENT SPEED
D_REF_VELOCIDAD_ACTUAL;Indicates the <b>CURRENT</b> speed of the primary circulation pump.

T_REF_ALTA_PRESION;FREIGHT PUMP | HIGH PRESSURE
D_REF_ALTA_PRESION;At least one freight pump cannot function due to high pressure.
T_REF_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;HIGH TEMPERATURE HAZARD
D_REF_ALTA_TEMPERATURA;If the light is on, it indicates that the module has exceeded operating temperature.<br>Too high a temperature level can cause a reduction in module efficiency, damage to the structure, or total destruction.
T_MonitorGenerador;TURBINE GENERATOR | MONITOR
D_MonitorGenerador;The monitor shows the main parameters and the current status of the turbine generators.
T_REF_CARGAR;COOLANT | LOAD
D_REF_CARGAR;It allows a controlled charge of 25% of coolant over the total capacity.
T_REF_PURGAR;COOLANT | PURGE
D_REF_PURGAR;It allows a controlled purge of 25% of coolant over the total capacity.
T_REF_CARGANDO;COOLANT | LOADING
D_REF_CARGANDO;The flashing light indicates that the pumps are loading coolant within the coolant circuit.
T_REF_PURGANDO;COOLANT | PURGING
D_REF_PURGANDO;The flashing light indicates that the pumps are purging coolant into the coolant circuit.
T_Interruptor_REF_INICIAR_CIRCULACION;PRIMARY CIRCUIT PUMP SWITCHES
D_Interruptor_REF_INICIAR_CIRCULACION;These pumps circulate water around the primary circuit.<br><br>This circulation allows hot core water to transfer its heat onto the steam generators. Core fuel cells may overheat if reactor core coolant water is not circulating.
T_Interruptor_CON_INICIAR_CIRCULACION;COOLING CIRCUIT PUMP
D_Interruptor_CON_INICIAR_CIRCULACION;Cooling circuit pump circulates water between the condenser and cooling towers.
T_Interruptor_REF_CARGAR_CORE_LOOP;PRIMARY CIRCUIT FREIGHT PUMP
D_Interruptor_REF_CARGAR_CORE_LOOP;This pump transfers water from the M03 Primary Circuit Storage Tank (CST) into the core vessel. This allows water to be loaded into the primary circuit.<br><br>Flashing lights indicate that the pump is overloaded or disabled for safety.
T_Interruptor_REF_CARGAR_CONDENSER_LOOP;SECONDARY CIRCUIT FREIGHT PUMP
D_Interruptor_REF_CARGAR_CONDENSER_LOOP;This pump moves water from the Cooling Towers into the condenser. This allows water to be loaded into the secondary circuit.<br><br>This switch is fed from an infinite source, so be careful not to overload the condenser. Flashing lights indicate that the pump is overloaded or disabled for safety. 
T_SEL_NUC_REF_EXTERNO;CORE POOL FREIGHT PUMP
D_SEL_NUC_REF_EXTERNO;This pump transfers coolant water to/from the M02 Core Pool Storage Tank and the Core Pool surrounding the reactor core.<br><br>Core Pool must be drained below the top of the reactor core to add/remove Fuel Cells and Control Rods.<br><br>Three red lights indicate that the pump is locked due to open floodgates/hatches.
T_REF_PRESION;COOLANT | PRESSURE
D_REF_PRESION;Indicator with the internal pressure of the reactor core coolant within the coolant circuit.<br>IMPORTANT: A pressure above the operating limit could cause loss of coolant, system degradation or even destruction of the circulation pumps.
T_REF_VOLUMEN_ACTUAL;COOLANT | CIRCULATING VOLUME
D_REF_VOLUMEN_ACTUAL;Indicator of the current volume of coolant inside the coolant circuit.<br>A volume lower than the operating limit could cause deficiencies in the cooling system, while a volume higher could dangerously increase the internal pressure within the circuit.

T_REF_VOLUMEN_DISPONIBLE;PRIMARY CIRCUIT STORAGE TANK | WATER LEVEL
D_REF_VOLUMEN_DISPONIBLE;Indicates the water level of the Primary Circuit Storage Tank (CST).
D_REF_ASIGNADO_B;COOLANT | SECONDARY PUMP
T_REF_VOL_SELECTOR;COOLANT ACTION SELECTOR
D_REF_VOL_SELECTOR;The selector is used to load or remove coolant from the cooling circuit.<br>IMPORTANT: The operating capacity of the cooling circuit could be exceeded if not properly monitored.
T_MonitorRefrigerante;REACTOR CORE COOLANT MONITOR
D_MonitorRefrigerante;The monitor shows the main parameters and the current status of the Reactor Core cooling system.
T_MOD_ESTADO_PRESENTE;MODERATOR | PRESENT
D_MOD_ESTADO_PRESENTE;The light on indicates that there is moderator available to load in the Reactor Core.
T_MOD_ESTADO_CARGANDO;MODERATOR | LOADING
D_MOD_ESTADO_CARGANDO;The flashing light indicates that the moderator is being loaded into the Reactor Core.
T_MOD_CARGAR;MODERATOR | LOAD
D_MOD_CARGAR;It allows a 25% moderator load on the total capacity.<br>IMPORTANT: Do not exceed the operating level as it could cause an increase in the internal pressure of the Reactor Core.
T_MOD_CANTIDAD_DISPONIBLE;MODERATOR | VOLUME IN RESERVE
D_MOD_CANTIDAD_DISPONIBLE;Indicator with the volume of moderator in the main reservoir, available for loading within the Reactor Core.
T_MOD_CANTIDAD;MODERATOR | VOLUME IN CORE
D_MOD_CANTIDAD;Indicator with the moderator volume in the Reactor Core.
T_MOD_PRESION;MODERATOR | PRESSURE
D_MOD_PRESION;Indicator with the internal pressure of the moderator within the Reactor Core circuit.<br>IMPORTANT: A pressure above the operating limit could cause loss of moderator, degradation of the system or even the destruction of the circulation pumps.
T_MonitorCombustible;REACTOR FUEL MONITOR
D_MonitorCombustible;The monitor shows the main parameters and the current fuel situation within the Reactor Core.
T_MOD_TEMPERATURA;MODERATOR | TEMPERATURE
D_MOD_TEMPERATURA;Indicator with the temperature of the moderator inside the circulation circuit.
T_MOD_PODERMODERACION;MODERATOR | FACTOR
D_MOD_PODERMODERACION;Indicator with the current fission moderation factor within the Reactor Core.<br>Too low a value indicates a weak moderation capacity, therefore the chain reaction will be unstable.
T_MOD_INTEGRIDAD;MODERATOR | INTEGRITY
D_MOD_INTEGRIDAD;The integrity of the moderator circuit can be degraded by wear or by exceeding operating parameters.<br>In either case, too low an integrity or too high a pressure can cause moderator losses.
T_COM_RESIDUOS_DESECHAR;WASTE | DISCARD
D_COM_RESIDUOS_DESECHAR;[BETA VERSION - FUNCTIONALITY NOT YET IMPLEMENTED]
T_PL_Residuos;Final Disposal Containers
D_PL_Residuos;The lights indicate the occupation of the final disposal containers.<br>Occupied containers can be cleaned during maintenance tasks.
T_PL_Combustible;FUEL CONTAINERS
D_PL_Combustible;The lights indicate the occupation of the fuel containers.<br>If there are empty containers, you will be able to buy new fuel cells to store.
T_COM_RESIDUOS_TEMPERATURA;WASTE | TEMPERATURE
D_COM_RESIDUOS_TEMPERATURA;[BETA VERSION - FUNCTIONALITY NOT YET IMPLEMENTED]
T_COM_ESTADO_RES_CARGA_CARGADO;WASTE | STATUS
D_COM_ESTADO_RES_CARGA_CARGADO;[BETA VERSION - FUNCTIONALITY NOT YET IMPLEMENTED]
T_COM_ESTADO_RES_CARGA_DESCARGADO;WASTE | DISCHARGED
D_COM_ESTADO_RES_CARGA_DESCARGADO;[BETA VERSION - FUNCTIONALITY NOT YET IMPLEMENTED]
T_MonitorAlarmas;ALARM MONITOR
D_MonitorAlarmas;The monitor displays active alarms.
T_MapaElectrico;INTERNAL ENERGY MONITOR
D_MapaElectrico;The monitor displays the current status of the internal power distribution.<br>Red color indicates that a module or cable is not energized.<br>Green indicates that a module or cable is energized.<br>Yellow indicates that there is a short in a trunk cable.
T_ALTERNAR_PUERTA;DOOR ACCESS
D_ALTERNAR_PUERTA;Press button to open or close door. Unpowered doors may need to be forced open with your hands.
T_SILENCIAR_ALARMAS;MUTE ALARMS
D_SILENCIAR_ALARMAS;Mutes active alarms and turns off red lighting.<br><br>Alarms may sound again if criticality is changed.
T_SEA_CAUDAL_01;COOLING TOWERS | CIRCULATION VALVE
D_SEA_CAUDAL_01;The valve controls the flow of coolant from the cooling circuit to the cooling towers.<br>By opening the valve, the coolant will be diverted for cooling.<br>Do not manually check if the emergency system motors are active.
T_SEA_CAUDAL_02;COOLING TOWERS | CIRCULATION VALVE
D_SEA_CAUDAL_02;The valve controls the flow of coolant from the cooling circuit to the cooling towers.<br>By opening the valve, the coolant will be diverted for cooling.<br>Do not manually check if the emergency system motors are active.
T_SEA_APERTURA_VALVULA_01;COOLING TOWERS | VALVE OPENING
D_SEA_APERTURA_VALVULA_01;Indicator with the degree of opening of the valve.
T_SEA_APERTURA_VALVULA_02;COOLING TOWERS | VALVE OPENING
D_SEA_APERTURA_VALVULA_02;Indicator with the degree of opening of the valve.
T_MesaMapa;OPERATIONAL MANAGEMENT TABLE
D_MesaMapa;The operational management table allows access to the different modules of the plant, to know their status, for their repair or replacement, or for the purchase or disposal of fuel.<br>It also allows you to manage the skills of the Operating Assistant.
T_BOMBA_DE_CIRCULACION;CIRCULATION PUMP
D_BOMBA_DE_CIRCULACION;Circulation pumps propel water in the primary, secondary, and cooling loops of a Pressurized Water Reactor (PWR).
T_BOMBA_DE_CARGA;FREIGHT PUMP
D_BOMBA_DE_CARGA;Freight pumps are designed to load water into a vessel.
T_CONTENEDOR;STORAGE TANK
D_CONTENEDOR;Storage tanks retain liquids or compressed gases for a future purpose.
D_EVAPORADOR;Steam generators boil water in the secondary system using hot, pressurized water in the primary system.
T_VALVULA;HYDRAULIC VALVES
D_VALVULA;Hydraulic valves regulate the flow of fluid. To operate manually, place valve into "BYPASS" mode to override signals from the control room.<br>Valve will require maintenance if stuck.
T_SEL_VALVULA;HYDRAULIC ACTUATOR
D_SEL_VALVULA;The hydraulic actuator allows the valves to be operated remotely. Set actuator to <b>OFF</b> position when the valve has reached the requested position.<br><br>If valve is stuck, maintenance will be required.
T_TAREA_DESECHAR_COMBUSTIBLE;DISCARD FUEL PROTOCOL
D_TAREA_DESECHAR_COMBUSTIBLE;Starts the used fuel disposal protocol.<br>The operational crane will be used to transport the fuel from the reactor core to the final disposal containers.
T_TAREA_CARGAR_COMBUSTIBLE;LOAD FUEL PROTOCOL
D_TAREA_CARGAR_COMBUSTIBLE;Starts the fueling protocol.<br>The operational crane will be used to transport the fuel cell from the containers to the reactor core.
T_SILENCIAR_ALARMA;ACKNOWLEDGE ALARMS
D_SILENCIAR_ALARMA;Press to silence active alarms and stop red lights.
T_Interruptor_PRE_CALENTADORES;PRESSURIZER HEATERS
D_Interruptor_PRE_CALENTADORES;Allows you to turn the Pressurizer heaters on or off.<br><br>Thermostat strongly recommended (<color=yellow>yellow</color> button to the left).
T_SEL_POWER_PRESURIZADOR;POWER SELECTOR 
D_SEL_POWER_PRESURIZADOR;Controls the amount of electric current through the Pressurizer heating coils.
T_LUZ_PRE_ENERGIA_INSUFICIENTE;PRESSURIZER HEATERS | ACTIVITY
D_LUZ_PRE_ENERGIA_INSUFICIENTE;Green light indicates that the heaters are operating at the requested heating power level.
T_BDC_PARADA;STOP CONTROL RODS
D_BDC_PARADA;Halts control rod movements.
T_BDC_SCRAM;SCRAM
D_BDC_SCRAM;Insert all control rods with maximum force.<br><br>The control rods can also be scrammed from the Control Rod Mechanical Room below the core. Each of the nine hydraulic pumps has manual SCRAM levers.
T_REF_TEMPERATURA_ENTRADA_NUCLEO;CORE INLET | TEMP
D_REF_TEMPERATURA_ENTRADA_NUCLEO;Indicates the water temperature at the reactor core vessel inlets.
T_REF_FACTOR_MODERACION;MODERATION LEVEL | PERCENT FILL
D_REF_FACTOR_MODERACION;Amount of water in the core divided by the total amount of water in the primary system.
T_REF_VOLUMEN_NUCLEO;REACTOR CORE | WATER LEVEL
D_REF_VOLUMEN_NUCLEO;Indicates the water level inside the reactor core. Ensure enough space for boric acid, if chemicals enabled. Never exceed 2500 m³ maximum capacity.
T_PRE_NIVEL_LLENADO;PRESSURIZER LEVEL | PERCENT FILL
D_PRE_NIVEL_LLENADO;Indicates volume of coolant in the Pressurizer as a percentage of maximum fill level. Operational values: 50-70%
T_REF_VOLUMEN_TOTAL;PRIMARY CIRCUIT | PERCENT FILL
D_REF_VOLUMEN_TOTAL;Indicates volume of coolant in the entire primary system as a percentage of maximum fill level.
T_REF_VOLUMEN_EXTERNO;CORE POOL | PERCENT FILL
D_REF_VOLUMEN_EXTERNO;Indicates the fill level of coolant in the core pool.<br><br>Hatches can be opened at about 50%.
T_REF_VOLUMEN_EXTERNO_TEMP;CORE POOL | TEMPERATURE
D_REF_VOLUMEN_EXTERNO_TEMP;Indicates the coolant temperature in the outer container of the reactor core.
T_TEMP_EVA;STEAM GENERATOR | SECONDARY CIRCUIT | WATER TEMP
D_TEMP_EVA;Indicates the water temperature inside the steam generator's Secondary Circuit.
T_PRESION_EVA;STEAM GENERATOR | SECONDARY CIRCUIT | STEAM PRESSURE
D_PRESION_EVA;Indicates the steam pressure inside the steam generator's Secondary Circuit.
T_VOLUMEN_EVA;STEAM GENERATOR | SECONDARY CIRCUIT | WATER LEVEL
D_VOLUMEN_EVA;Indicates the water level inside the steam generator's secondary circuit.
T_0_CON_VOLUMEN;CONDENSER | SECONDARY CIRCUIT | WATER LEVEL
D_0_CON_VOLUMEN;Indicates the water level inside the condenser.
T_0_CON_TEMPERATURA;CONDENSER | SECONDARY CIRCUIT | WATER TEMP
D_0_CON_TEMPERATURA;Indicates the water temperature inside the condenser's Secondary Circuit.
T_0_CON_PRESION;CONDENSER | SECONDARY CIRCUIT | PRESSURE
D_0_CON_PRESION;Indicates the pressure or vacuum inside the steam generator's Secondary Circuit.
T_REF_BOMBA_AGUA_OVERLOAD;FREIGHT PUMP | HIGH VOLUME
D_REF_BOMBA_AGUA_OVERLOAD;Indicates that the freight pump is running above its capacity.<br>There is no more space within the circuit to continue pumping and the pressure exceeds the propulsion capacity of the pump.
T_REF_MANTENIMIENTO;FREIGHT PUMP | MAINTENANCE REQUIRED
D_REF_MANTENIMIENTO;At least one freight pump requires maintenance.
T_GEIGER_COUNTER;GEIGER COUNTER
D_GEIGER_COUNTER;Geiger counters can tell you there is radiation around you, but it can’t tell you the original source of the radiation, what type it is or how much energy it contains.
T_CajaPanelBombasCirculacionCondensador;PUMP STATUS COLOR CODE
D_CajaPanelBombasCirculacionCondensador;GREY - Disconnected<br>WHITE - Connected<br>YELLOW - Reaching Ordered Speed<br>GREEN - Ordered Speed Reached
T_CajaPanelEvaporadoresInstalados;STEAM GENERATORS INSTALLED
D_CajaPanelEvaporadoresInstalados;The panel lights indicate the steam generators installed in the plant.
T_CajaPanelBombasCirculacion;PUMP STATUS COLOR CODE
D_CajaPanelBombasCirculacion;GREY - Disconnected<br>WHITE - Connected<br>YELLOW - Reaching Ordered Speed<br>GREEN - Ordered Speed Reached
T_REF_VEL_SET_SLOW;PRIMARY CIRCUIT PUMP SPEED
D_REF_VEL_SET_SLOW;Orders the primary circuit pumps to 25%.
T_REF_VEL_SET_MED;PRIMARY CIRCUIT PUMP SPEED
D_REF_VEL_SET_MED;Orders the primary circuit pumps to 50%.
T_REF_VEL_SET_FAST;PRIMARY CIRCUIT PUMP SPEED
D_REF_VEL_SET_FAST;Orders the primary circuit pumps to 100%.
T_CON_CIRC_VEL_SET_SLOW;SECONDARY PUMP SPEED - 25%
D_CON_CIRC_VEL_SET_SLOW;Orders the secondary circuit pumps to 25%.
T_CON_CIRC_VEL_SET_MED;SECONDARY PUMP SPEED - 50%
D_CON_CIRC_VEL_SET_MED;Orders the secondary circuit pumps to 50%.
T_CON_CIRC_VEL_SET_FAST;SECONDARY PUMP SPEED - 100%
D_CON_CIRC_VEL_SET_FAST;Orders the secondary circuit pumps to 100%.
T_REG_CON_CIRCULACION;SECONDARY PUMP SPEED - SET
D_REG_CON_CIRCULACION;Orders the secondary circuit pumps to a user-selectable speed.
T_CON_VEL_SET_SLOW;COOLING PUMP SPEED - 25%
D_CON_VEL_SET_SLOW;Orders the cooling circuit pump to 25%.
T_CON_VEL_SET_MED;COOLING PUMP SPEED - 50%
D_CON_VEL_SET_MED;Orders the cooling circuit pump to 50%.
T_CON_VEL_SET_FAST;COOLING PUMP SPEED - 100%
D_CON_VEL_SET_FAST;Orders the cooling circuit pump to 100%.
T_REG_CON_ENFRIAMIENTO;COOLING PUMP SPEED - SET
D_REG_CON_ENFRIAMIENTO;Orders the cooling circuit pump to a user-selectable speed.
T_CALENTADOR_PRESURIZADOR;PRESSURIZER HEATERS
D_CALENTADOR_PRESURIZADOR;The heaters are responsible for supplying the necessary thermal energy to maintain the water temperature in the pressurizer at a constant level, which helps prevent pressure fluctuations and ensures safe and stable operation of the reactor
T_BOMBA_DE_VACIO;ELECTRIC VACUUM PUMP
D_BOMBA_DE_VACIO;The electric vacuum pump creates a vacuum in the condenser. It is especially useful when the Steam Jet Ejector cannot yet produce a strong enough vacuum.
T_PRESURIZADOR;PRESSURIZER
D_PRESURIZADOR;Pressurizer maintains the pressure in the primary coolant loop, which is essential for efficient heat transfer and to prevent the coolant from boiling.
T_TRAJE_PROTECTOR;HAZMAT SUIT
D_TRAJE_PROTECTOR;Protective suits allow you to work in radiation-contaminated areas without being damaged by radioactivity.
D_TURBINA_GENERADORA;The steam produced by the reactor's primary cooling system is sent to the turbines, causing them to spin.
D_TURBINA_ELECTRICA;As the turbine spins, it turns a generator which produces alternating current electricity.
T_RECARGA_ELECTROGENOS;Monitoring of diesel generators
