Debug_Descripcion;Activating this option can cause data loss and other strange behavior during the game.<br><b>DO NOT ACTIVATE IT IF IT WAS NOT DIRECTLY REQUESTED BY THE DEVELOPER.</b>
LIMPIAR_REPORTE_MANTENIMIENTO;This action will erase the current maintenance report.
S_Idioma_Voces;Interface language and subtitles.
T_Subtitulos;Show or hide subtitles when there are dialogues.
S_EventosVisuales;Visual events are important warnings of situations that occur within the plant.
T_ToolTips;Shows the possible actions to perform on an object or control.
T_AyudaEnZona;Shows visual indicators in specific areas with explanations and information.
T_EstadisticasEnMemoria;Keeps stats in memory to improve game performance, but increases memory consumption.
T_EnviarLog;In case of error, the game will automatically send an error report to the developer.
T_InputAlternativo;Activates alternate character control.<br>Activate if the character moves erratically with normal control.
T_FullScreen;Enable or disable full screen support.
T_AyudaRefresco;Enables continuous updating of the values shown in the meter tooltip.<br><br>You no longer need to tap the gauge for updated readings.
Slider_SensibilidadZoom;Allows you to modify the movement of the pointer in short distances.<br>Adjust to improve precision.
Slider_Velocidad;Maximum speed that the cursor can reach.
T_Compensacion;Dampens pointer movements for smoother changes of direction.
T_MedidoresAnimados;Activate smooth gauge movement for all gauges at all times.<br>May affect performance.<br><br>When disabled, the game will activate smooth gauge movement when possible.
T_RecordarUltimoZoom;The player can zoom in using the Right Mouse Button and change the zoom by scrolling the mouse wheel.<br><br>When enabled, the game will remember the last zoom setting.
T_EfectosFisicos;Displays detailed particles, smoke and explosion details.
T_EfectosAtmosfericos;Displays detailed humidity, dust and environmental particles.
T_EfectosAOMejorado;Displays shadows on the edges of objects (ambient occlusion).
T_ReflejosDinamicos;Enables reflections that change based on active lights.
T_EfectoEyeAdaptation;Enables automatic exposure adjustment when transitioning between bright and dark environments.
T_EfectoMotionBlur;Blurs the camera during fast movements.
T_EfectoProfundidadDeCampo;Enables dynamic Depth Of Field photographic effect.
T_AguaSimulada;Shows animated reflecting pools and advanced fluid simulation.
T_EventosRandom;Enable random failures.<br>(Experienced Players Only)
T_Clima;When enabled, outside weather will affect the condenser's performance.<br>Note: This may stop water vapor from appearing above the cooling towers.
T_AnimacionAlCaminar;Sways the camera according to the player's body movements.<br>Can cause some players to get dizzy.
T_ModuloQuimico;If active, gameplay will include chemicals such as Boron, NaOH, Iodine, and Xenon.<br>Not recommended for brand-new players.
T_Slider_EventosRandom;Select frequency of events and disasters.<br>High values increase the risk of uncontrolled disaster.
Slider_EventosRandom;Select frequency of events and disasters.<br>High values increase the risk of uncontrolled disaster.
DIALOGO_SALIDA_TREN_TITULO;Return to Main Menu
DIALOGO_SALIDA_TREN_DESCRIPCION;This button allows you to escape an imminent meltdown. However, since there is no emergency, pressing ACCEPT will return you to MAIN MENU with no change in prestige points. You can also hit CANCEL, return to the plant, and save your progress before exiting the game. It's time to choose.
APP_AYUDA_1;Prestige Points
APP_AYUDA_D_1;"Prestige Points" are the in-game currency of this game. You will earn points for each hour and day in which you meet the city's energy demands, plus additional points for optional, randomly-issued objectives.<br><br>You start each new game with 2,000 points. On the first game day, you can also earn additional points for turning on AO and by visiting various locations in the plant.<br><br>You can use these points to order services and supplies for the facility. You can perform your own maintenance scans around the facility, and task AO to repair and maintain the equipment and facility infrastructure.<br><br>Once you advance your Operator Level and accumulate a large amount of Prestige Points, you can upgrade your existing equipment and buy more powerful equipment using Prestige Points. If you haven't yet earned the necessary points, you can take up to two loans in the tablet's BANK AND INVOICES app.
APP_AYUDA_0;Objective and Events
APP_AYUDA_D_0;Your primary objective is to ensure the efficient and safe operation of the Nucleares Power Plant while meeting the city's demand for electrical power. This requires careful consideration and maintenance of the reactor to balance safety and operational demands.<br><br>To avoid any major issues, it's best to maintain the reactor within normal parameters and conduct necessary maintenance in a timely manner. Additionally, there may be optional events that you can participate in to earn Prestige Points. These are great opportunities to showcase your skills and earn recognition for your efforts.<br><br>Although you may be tempted to push the reactor beyond its operational limits, it's important to exercise caution as this could have severe consequences. Keep the reactor running smoothly and seize any chance to earn <b>Prestige Points!</b>
APP_AYUDA_2;Operating Licenses
APP_AYUDA_D_2;An operational license is a permit to operate the reactor.<br><br>At the start, you are granted five operational licenses. Once you run out of licenses, you will no longer be authorized to operate the reactor, and the game will end.<br><br>The license indicator is located at the top center of the screen. You will lose one operating license if you fail to meet the minimum service level for two consecutive days. Licenses will turn yellow if in jeopardy of being revoked. However, if you meet the service level requirement, you will regain the lost license.<br><br>You may also lose a license if significant irregularities are detected during an inspection by agents from the National Atomic Energy Commission (NAEC).
APP_AYUDA_3;Emergency Escape Plan
APP_AYUDA_D_3;The plant is designed with numerous redundancies to avoid a serious accident. Nevertheless, it's still possible for you to damage the plant to the point of its destruction. At that point, a timer will appear on screen before the plant explodes. You will have at least 3 options:<br><br><b>Option 1: Reverse the Meltdown.</b> See the separate article titled "Reverse Meltdown Minigame". If successful, you will earn the "Reversed Meltdown" Steam Achievement.<br><br><b>Option 2: Train Escape!</b> Exit the facility, board the train, activate the power, release the brakes, and press <color=red>ESCAPE</color>. If you escape before the plant explodes, you can start a new game with approximately 50% of your previous level, experience, and prestige points. You will also earn the "Train Escape" Steam Achievement.<br><br><b>Option 3: Game Over!</b> If the timer runs out and you haven't stopped the meltdown and haven't escaped, the plant will be destroyed in a fiery explosion. The game will be over, and you will earn the "Reactor Destroyer" Steam Achievement.
FISION_REVERTIDA;MELTDOWN REVERSED
AVISO_PARADA_EMERGENCIA_TITULO;Emergency Stop
AVISO_PARADA_EMERGENCIA;Emergency Stop@In the new version significant changes have been made to the simulator engine.<br><br>The progress has been uploaded, but for safety, the plant is in an emergency stop.<br><br>It is recommended to read the patch notes before attempting to power up the reactor.@AYUDA_CONTROL_NUCLEO
