APP_AYUDA_6;Transformers
APP_AYUDA_D_6;Transformers reduce the amount of wasted electricity in the electrical grid by allowing transmission lines to operate under much higher voltages. In contrast, power plants, factories, and homes operate with much lower voltages.<br><br>The Nucleares plant provides space for three (3) step-up transformers to be installed in parallel. You can choose among three separate transformer model classes based on your demand needs.<br><br>When you coordinate the plant's startup or shutdown with the city grid operator, the city will activate the plant's transformers during the approved hours. If you underdeliver or overdeliver power to the grid, the city may disable your transformers to protect the integrity of the grid.<br><br>See the topic entry on "Excess Power Generation".
APP_AYUDA_7;Excess power generation
APP_AYUDA_D_7;In this game, undelivered power can cause overheating, leading to smoke, fire, and destruction of the electrical components. This applies in two ways.<br><br><b>1. Internal Distribution:</b> Diesel Generators can overheat and be destroyed if operating with no electrical load. The plant can automatically start diesel generators; however, it is your responsibility to turn them off when there are other available energy sources.<br><br>2. External Distribution: The Resistor Banks and Turbine Generators can overheat and be destroyed if operating with excessive load. Always ensure that the plant is delivering power through the Transformers, and never produce more power than your Resistor Banks can dissipate.<br><br>See the topic entry on "Transformers".
T_TRANSFORMADOR;Transformer
D_TRANSFORMADOR;Raises the voltage of the generated energy for subsequent distribution.
T_REPUESTO_RESISTOR;Resistor block
D_REPUESTO_RESISTOR;Resistance block that the resistor bank uses internally to absorb the excess energy generated.
T_BANCO_RESISTOR;Resistor Bank
D_BANCO_RESISTOR;It can absorb the surplus energy generated.
FIN_DEL_REPORTE;<b><br><br>==== END OF REPORT ====</b>
