D_GEN_TORQUE_TURBINA;Amount of rotational force applied to the turbine.
T_TE_TORQUE_MINIMO;Minimum Torque Reached
D_TE_TORQUE_MINIMO;Torque meets the minimum threshold to generate power.
T_TE_RPM_ESTABLE;STABLE TURBINE RPM
D_TE_RPM_ESTABLE;Turbine is maintaining a consistent speed. Ensure lamp is illuminated before using the synchroscope.
T_Interruptor_Link_TurBypass;BYPASS VALVE LINK
D_Interruptor_Link_TurBypass;Adjusts all valves simultaneously based on the setting of one valve. Disable for independent control.
T_CajaSyncroscopio;SYNCHROSCOPE
D_CajaSyncroscopio;The synchroscope compares the turbine generator's frequency and phase to the city power grid. Just before connecting to the grid, you can RAISE and LOWER the turbine's RPM so that the two alternating currents are aligned. Severe damage to the plant can occur if the transformers are connected out-of-phase with the grid. If the synchroscope suddenly starts clicking, you need to take action to prevent undelivered power from damaging the resistor banks and turbine generator.
AYUDA_CONTROL_SINCROSCOPIO_TITULO;SYNCHROSCOPE
AYUDA_CONTROL_SINCROSCOPIO;SYNCHROSCOPE@The synchroscope compares the turbine generator's frequency and phase to the city power grid. The synchroscope clicks every time the plant's phase lines up with the grid's phase.<br><br>Just before connecting to the grid, you can RAISE and LOWER the turbine's RPM so that the two alternating currents are aligned. Severe damage to the plant can occur if the transformers are connected out-of-phase with the grid.<br><br>Once both alternating currents are in phase (i.e., the crests of their sine waves are aligned with each other), both red dots will turn green. This indicates that you can safely CLOSE the breaker that connects the plant to the city grid.<br><br>The synchroscope monitors the plant and grid at all times. If you hear the synchroscope suddenly clicking, you need to take action to prevent undelivered power from damaging the resistor banks and turbine generator.@AYUDA_CONTROL_NUCLEO
