D_MD_Volumen_Residuos;This tank contains waste fluids. Due to its toxic contents, it can only be cleaned by AO.
T_MD_pH;PRIMARY CIRCUIT | pH
D_MD_pH;pH affects Boron's absorption capacity. The operating range is between 7 and 9. Low pH values indicate acidity that can increase corrosion of the pipes.
T_Medidor_CAPACIDAD_ABSORCION_IONES;ION EXCHANGER | ABSORPTION CAPACITY
D_Medidor_CAPACIDAD_ABSORCION_IONES;The Ion Exchanger's absorption capacity decreases with use.<br><br>Absorption capacity can be restored by using the <b>ION EXCHANGE CLEANING SYSTEM</b> located in the Chemical Treatment Room.
T_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_SAL_COL_IONES;Ion Exchanger Outlet Valve
D_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_SAL_COL_IONES;To allow boron to be filtered from the primary circuit, both the inlet and outlet valves must be open.<br><br>Note: This is a manual valve which can only be operated from the Chemical Treatment Room. Temperature impacts are not modeled.
T_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_ENT_COL_IONES;Ion Exchanger Inlet Valve
D_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_ENT_COL_IONES;To allow boron to be filtered from the primary circuit, both the inlet and outlet valves must be open.<br><br>Note: This is a manual valve which can only be operated from the Chemical Treatment Room. Temperature impacts are not modeled.
T_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_SALIDA_NaOH;NaOH Tank Valve
D_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_SALIDA_NaOH;The alert light indicates that the outlet valve of the sodium hydroxide reserve tank is open.<br>Open only for maintenance tasks.
T_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_SALIDA_Agua;M01 Water Valve
D_LUZ_Q_VALVULA_SALIDA_Agua;The alert light indicates that the outlet valve of the water reserve tank is open.
T_NUC_BORO;Boronometer
D_NUC_BORO;Measures boron in the core. After initial dosing into the core, this value will decrease as boron is diluted throughout the primary circuit.
