MAQUINA_DESCRIPCION_BARRA_DE_CONTROL;Nuclear fission occurs in the reactor core when a thermal neutron collides with the nucleus of a uranium atom.<br>The uranium atom splits into daughter products and ejects 2 to 3 new neutrons, creating a sustained chain reaction.<br>Control rods absorb these excess neutrons to maintain a stable power level.<br><br>Control rods can be inserted from 0% (fully withdrawn from the core) to 100% (fully inserted in the core).<br>When using the in-game control rod keypad, you can use the mouse, enter values on the numeric keypad and press [ENTER], or press the - (Minus) and + (Plus) keys to adjust in steps of one tenth of a percent.<br>Additionally, press [SHIFT] to bypass animation if enabled in menu options.
