START_VERSION;V 2.2.25.219 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_0;Welcome to <b>Nucleares</b>. This tutorial walks you through a cold start until you connect power to the city.<br><br>Remember this plant model: a <b>Primary</b> circuit carries heat from the core, a <b>Secondary</b> circuit turns that heat into steam for the turbine, and a <b>Cooling</b> circuit rejects leftover heat. Your job after startup is to match the city's power demand without damaging equipment.<br><br>Most controls are locked until you finish. Then you can play freely and save.<br><br><b>Toggle [H] for hotkeys. Press [ENTER] to continue.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_1;First, power every control station. Without power, gauges stay dark and you cannot see what the plant is doing.<br><br>From this Control Room you will monitor pressure, temperature, flow, vacuum, and power output at all times.<br><br><b>Activate the power levers on each control station.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_2;Walk the Control Room and learn the layout: reactor/fuel and pressurizer on one side, pumps and steam systems in the middle, turbine sync and power delivery on the other.<br><br><b>Right-click</b> most controls and gauges for a short explanation. Use this often - it is the fastest way to learn what each panel does.<br><br><b>Press [ENTER] when you're ready to proceed.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_3;The plant needs electrical power before anything else runs. The nearby city sells <b>External Power</b> cheaply. The Diesel Generator burns fuel and is mainly a backup. If both fail, emergency batteries keep critical systems alive for a short time.<br><br>Watch the power indicators as you switch sources - knowing where plant power comes from is a core skill.<br><br>1. Turn <color=red>OFF</color> the Diesel Generator.<br><br>2. Watch how the plant switches to emergency battery backup.<br><br>3. Turn on the <color=green>External Power Supply</color>.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_4;Next, prepare the <b>Primary</b> circuit. Water in this loop must stay pressurized so it does not boil in the core. The Pressurizer (PZR) heaters raise that pressure; its <color=yellow>thermostat</color> prevents overheating.<br><br>Watch the primary pressure gauge climb. High pressure is what lets the primary carry heat safely to the Steam Generators.<br><br><b>1. Turn on the <color=yellow>Thermostat.</color></b><br><br><b>2. Turn on <color=red>Heaters</color>.</b><br><br>3. Wait for primary circuit pressure to reach {0} BAR.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_5;The <b>Primary</b> circuit of a Pressurized Water Reactor (PWR) circulates pressurized hot water between the core and the Steam Generators. Pump speed controls how much heat leaves the core - later, this is one of your main power levers.<br><br>We start only the 3rd loop for this tutorial.<br><br><b>1. <color=red>START</color> the 3rd Primary Circulation Pump.<br><br>2. Set its speed to {0}% and wait for pump to reach ordered value.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_6;The <b>Cooling</b> circuit moves heat from the Condenser to the Cooling Towers and dumps it outdoors. Without cooling flow, condenser pressure and temperature rise and the plant cannot reject heat.<br><br><b>1. <color=red>START</color> the Cooling Circuit pump.<br><br>2. Set its speed to {0}% and wait for pump to reach ordered value.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_6_C01;The <b>Vacuum System</b> lowers Condenser pressure so steam can condense efficiently. Low condenser pressure is also required before the turbine can run safely.<br><br>For startup we feed the ejector with bypass steam. Hold [ALT] to spin dials faster.<br><br>1. To the right, set the <b>Startup Motive Steam Inlet (SMSI) to 100%.</b><br><br>2. To the left of the Synchroscope, set the 3rd <b>Bypass Valve to 100%.<br><br>3. Wait for both valves to reach ordered values.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_6B;Good. Before you can sell power, the city grid operator must approve operations. After approval, the city sends a demand target - matching that demand is the main gameplay loop once you are online.<br><br>Your Tablet ([TAB]) is also where you will find Help, communications, and other plant tools after the tutorial.<br><br><b>1. Activate your Tablet.</b> [TAB key]<br><br><b>2. Click "COM" icon.</b><br><br><b>3. Click "Start Operations" and wait to receive a start time.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_6C;You have approval. Early on, the generator can produce more power than the city asks for. Extra electrical load must go somewhere or equipment overheats.<br><br><b>Resistor banks absorb surplus power.</b> Later you will balance city demand, resistors, and reactor output together.<br><br><b>1. Connect the <color=red>01 Resistor Bank</color> so that the generator doesn\'t overheat.</b><br><br>2. Notice how the "01" white "Connected Resistor Bank" indicator turns <color=green>green</color>.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_7;Excellent. Fuel must be loaded and the plant set to an operating mode before fission can begin. After the reaction starts, conditions change quickly - form the habit of checking gauges before each major action.<br><br>1. Walk left to the <b>FUEL</b> panel.<br><br>2. Set the plant's Operating Mode to <b>NOMINAL</b>.<br><br>3. Press <b><color=red>LOWER PISTON</color></b>.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_8;Control rods absorb neutrons. At 100% inserted they stop fission. Withdrawing them allows the chain reaction to start. Rod position is your main reactivity control - raise fission carefully, never all at once outside procedures.<br><br>In an emergency, press <color=red><b>EMERGENCY STOP</b></color> or <color=red><b>SCRAM</b></color> to fully insert the rods. This works even if the Control Room loses power.<br><br>To initiate fission, <b>withdraw the control rods to {0}%.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_9;Excellent! The chain reaction has begun. Wait for the reactor to reach <b>critical mass</b> - the point where fission becomes self-sustaining and core heat rises on its own.<br><br>Watch core status and temperature while you wait. After this, heat will move into the Steam Generators.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_10;The reactor is now reactive. Primary water is carrying core heat into the Steam Generators.<br><br>On the right panel, watch Steam Generator <b>pressure</b>, <b>temperature</b>, and <b>water level</b>. At about 100°C, secondary water boils into steam: level falls and pressure rises. That steam will later spin the turbine.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_11;The <b>Secondary Circuit</b> is a Rankine cycle: water moves through the <b>pump</b>, boils in the <b>Steam Generator</b>, can drive the <b>turbine</b>, then returns via the <b>condenser</b>. Primary and secondary water never mix - only heat crosses.<br><br><b>1. <color=red>START</color> the Secondary Circuit Pump.<br><br>2. Set its speed to {0}% and wait for pump to reach ordered value.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_12;Recap - all three circuits are flowing:<br>- <b>Primary:</b> core heat → Steam Generators<br>- <b>Secondary:</b> steam (now on bypass) → Condenser<br>- <b>Cooling:</b> Condenser heat → Cooling Towers<br><br>Your two long-term controls will be <b>control rods</b> (how much heat the core makes) and <b>primary pump speed</b> (how much heat you send out). Next we build vacuum so the turbine can start safely.<br><br><b>Press [ENTER] to continue.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_12_C2;Vacuum: BYPASS and SMSI already feed the Steam Jet Ejector, but at low power it cannot pull a strong enough vacuum alone.<br><br>When the Retention Tank is full enough, the Electric Vacuum Pump can finish the job. Rule to remember forever: <b>never run the turbine without condenser vacuum.</b><br><br><b>1. Wait for the Retention Tank to reach {0}% so you can use the Electric Vacuum Pump.<br><br>2. While waiting, try changing the game speed. [T], [0], [1], [2], [3], [P]</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_12_C2B;The Electric Vacuum Pump uses Retention Tank water at high speed to pull condenser pressure down when the ejector is not enough.<br><br>Watch the condenser PRESSURE gauge - lower is better here.<br><br><b>1. Turn <color=green>ON</color> the Electric Vacuum Pump.<br><br>2. Wait for the PRESSURE gauge to indicate 0.1 BAR.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_12_C3;<b>Survival rule:</b> keep condenser vacuum whenever steam can reach the turbine (Main Steam Control Valve open, or similar steam path).<br><br>Spinning the turbine without vacuum - even once - will eventually destroy it. If vacuum is lost later, close steam to the turbine first, then recover vacuum.<br><br><b>Press [ENTER] to continue.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_12_C4;Next you will move steam from bypass into the turbine. Closing the bypass cuts SMSI steam, so you must switch the vacuum ejector to <b>Operational Motive Steam Inlet (OMSI)</b>, which uses turbine steam instead of startup steam.<br><br>Read the next checklist carefully before you touch the valves.<br><br><b>Press [ENTER] when ready.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_12_C5;Start the turbine by switching vacuum motive steam and sending bypass steam into the turbine path. Do these in order.<br><br><b>1. Change electric pump mode to Operational Mode.<br><br>2. Close SMSI to 0%.<br><br>3. Open OMSI to {0}%.<br><br>4. Close the 3rd BYPASS valve to 0%.</b>

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_13;Your main operating levers are unlocked:<br><br>- <b>CONTROL RODS</b> numpad - more withdrawn = more fission and core heat.<br>- <b>PRIMARY PUMP</b> speed - faster = more heat sent to the Steam Generators, turbine, and resistors.<br><br>After the tutorial, use both to follow city demand. Too much output without enough load damages equipment.<br><br>The game will advance when ready.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_13B;Your main operating levers are unlocked:<br><br>- <b>CONTROL RODS</b> numpad - more withdrawn = more fission and core heat.<br>- <b>PRIMARY PUMP</b> speed - faster = more heat sent to the Steam Generators, turbine, and resistors.<br><br>After the tutorial, use both to follow city demand. Too much output without enough load damages equipment.<br><br>Press [ENTER] to continue.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_14;The turbine is accelerating toward about 3060 RPM. Watch the synchroscope: it ticks when the generator is in phase with the city grid.<br><br>Connecting out of phase can destroy the generator. Next you will match phase, voltage, and frequency, then close the breaker.<br><br>Press [ENTER] to continue.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_15;Good. Allow the turbine to accelerate closer to 3060 RPM before synchronizing it to the grid. Watch RPM and the synchroscope - do not rush the breaker.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_15A;<color=red>Warning!</color> Turbine power exceeds what the resistor banks can absorb. Surplus power with nowhere to go damages resistors or generators.<br><br><b>Fix:</b> reduce fission or heat transfer - enter a larger number in the CONTROL ROD numpad or decrease PRIMARY PUMP speed.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_15B;RPM is stable but the generator is still <b>out of phase</b> with the grid. Closing the breaker now would be catastrophic.<br><br>Press RPM RAISE and LOWER until both red dots are aligned together. When the generator is in phase, both dots will turn <color=green>green</color>.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_15C;Perfect! Now adjust Voltage and Hertz so turbine output matches what the city needs. Voltage does not have to be exact; frequency and phase matter more.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_15D;You're almost there! Use the RPM Raise/Lower buttons to align the red dots together. Wait for a stable green phase before you close the breaker.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_15E;<b><color=red>CLOSE</color> the Circuit Breaker now.</b><br>Phase is good - connect to the city grid.

TUTORIAL_INICIO_PASO_16;<b>CONGRATULATIONS!</b> The plant is online.<br><br><b>What to do now:</b><br>1. Watch city demand and keep your output close to it (rods + primary pumps + resistors).<br>2. Protect vacuum, pressure, and temperatures - alarms mean stop and diagnose.<br>3. Press [C] for the startup Checklist, [TAB] for Tablet Help, and right-click any control you do not recognize.<br><br>You can explore the plant, use all Control Room controls, and save. From the Main Menu you can start a new game or rerun this tutorial.<br><br>Core rules: <b>match demand</b>, <b>never turbine without vacuum</b>, <b>never generate more than you can absorb</b>. Experiment, learn from mistakes, and have fun!

